</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Set Arrival Time and Departure Time to required. The expense item uses rate table conditions based on start or end travel times.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Set Arrival Time and Departure Time to required. The expense item uses rate table conditions based on start or end travel times.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>You can only select Expense Accumulator on fixed expense items that use an expense rate table.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can only select Expense Accumulator on fixed expense items that use an expense rate table.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Select either Item Unit Price or Expense Rate Table for the expense item.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Select either Item Unit Price or Expense Rate Table for the expense item.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>You can’t specify distance-based expense items as child expense items.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can’t specify distance-based expense items as child expense items.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>"[rate_table_name]" is in use as an adjustment rate table and can't also be used as a base rate table.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't use rate tables based on percentages as base rate tables.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Select the Require Distance Calculation Attributes on Expense Reports check box. The expense rate table is using the Estimated Distance of Driving Route expense item attribute.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Select the Require Distance Calculation Attributes on Spend Authorizations check box. The expense rate table is using the Estimated Distance of Driving Route expense item attribute.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The associated expense rate table is using the [trip distance] expense item attribute. Ensure that you select the Enable for Spend Authorizations check box on the [trip distance] attribute.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The associated expense rate table is using the [trip distance] expense item attribute. Ensure that you select the Enable for Expense Reports check box on the [trip distance] attribute.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't select [trip distance] on expense items if the associated rate table doesn't include 1 of these attributes as an attribute to evaluate: Distance to Expense, Estimated Distance of Driving Route, or [trip distance].</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The associated expense rate table is using the Distance to Expense expense item attribute. Ensure that you select the Enable for Expense Reports check box on the One-Way Daily Commute or Round Trip attributes.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
