</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't select One-Way Daily Commute on expense items if the associated rate table doesn't use 1 of these attributes as an attribute to evaluate: Distance to Expense, Estimated Distance of Driving Route, or [trip distance].</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The associated expense rate table is using the Distance to Expense expense item attribute. Ensure that you select the Enable for Spend Authorizations check box on the One-Way Daily Commute or Round Trip attributes.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't select Estimated Distance of Driving Route on expense items if the associated rate table doesn't include 1 of these attributes as an attribute to evaluate: Distance to Expense, Estimated Distance of Driving Route, or [trip distance].</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>To use the new functionality, you must use web service v43.0 or later. You can use the enhanced web services to set expense item configurations: * For charge breakdowns on itemization lines. * To automatically populate itemization lines from credit card transactions. * To configure 7 or more itemization mapping lines. * To use itemization mapping for expenses other than hotel expenses.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Arrival Date and Departure Date Expense Item Attributes need to be set to required for a Hotel Itemization Expense Item.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Arrival Date and Departure Date Expense Item Attributes need to be set to required for a Hotel Itemization Expense Item.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>You can't set both Hotel Itemization and Hide Itemization to true on an expense item.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't set both Hotel Itemization and Hide Itemization to true on an expense item.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>You can’t set Hide Itemization to true if hotel itemization mappings exist.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can’t set Hide Itemization to true if hotel itemization mappings exist.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>You can’t set both Enable Travel Journal and Hide Itemization to true on an expense item.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can’t set both Enable Travel Journal and Hide Itemization to true on an expense item.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>You can’t set Hide Itemization to true if itemization mappings exist.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can’t set Hide Itemization to true if itemization mappings exist.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Expense_Item_ID" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Expense Item ID. This is the Expense Item unique identifier</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Item_Name" type="xsd:string" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Free form text field for meaningful Expense Item Name</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Expense Item Name is already used.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Expense Item Name is already used.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Resource_Category_Reference" type="wd:Spend_CategoryObjectType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>This is the reference id value of the spend category. A spend category is a classification of items and services that drive the accounting. All expense items are associated with a Spend Category and sales items are associated with a Revenue Category.If a value is provided for sales item, revenue category will default so it is recommended to provide a value for either sales item or revenue category but not both. It is required if sales item is blank.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Item_Description" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Free form text field to provide detailed description of the Expense Item</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Synonyms_and_Keywords" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Synonyms and Key words which are similar to the Expense Item name. These will allow an infrequent user to type in something reasonable and find the correct expense item.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Per_Diem_Expense" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Boolean flag indicating if the Expense Item is a Per Diem Expense. Used for reporting purposes only.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Item_Unit_Price" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Currency field for Item Unit Price</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Unit Price must be greater than or equal to zero.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Currency_Reference" type="wd:CurrencyObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to the currency of the company. If entered, this field is not processed on inbound Workday Web Services requests.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Common_Reference_ID_Type>Currency_ID</wd:Common_Reference_ID_Type>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Instructional_Text" type="wd:RichText" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Free form Rich Text field to enter instructions for users creating expense reports.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Expense_Policy_Group_Reference" type="wd:Expense_Policy_GroupObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to an existing Expense Policy Group. Assigning expense item to policy groups is done to make it easier for an administrator to search for and select items for segmented security setup.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Expense_Item_Group_Reference" type="wd:Expense_Item_GroupObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to an existing Expense Item Group. Assigning expense items to item groups is done to make it easier to search for and select items. Expense items can belong to multiple groups.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Job_Profile_Reference" type="wd:Job_ProfileObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to an existing Job Profile. Workers in this Job Profile can use this Expense Item.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Unit_of_Measure_Reference" type="wd:Unit_of_MeasureObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to an existing Unit of Measure</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Tax_Applicability_Configuration_Data" type="wd:Tax_Applicability_Configuration_DataType" minOccurs="0"/>
<xsd:element name="Travel_Journal" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>This boolean will enable travel journal entry on the expense report line.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Specify expense items that are either distance-based or per diems and travel journals, not both.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Travel_Journal_Item_Reference" type="wd:Expense_ItemObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Expense Item used for daily travel journal entry.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Travel_Journal_Type_Reference" type="wd:Travel_Journal_TypeObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Defines Travel Journal configuration type for Expense Item.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't modify the travel journal configuration of expense items when they're in use on expense reports.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Rounding_Option_for_Hours_Reference" type="wd:Rounding_OptionObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Rounding option for the "Number of Hours" attribute defined on TJ Expense Item</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Non_Editable_Number_of_Hours" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>This boolean will make the Number of Hours not enterable on the Travel Journal lines.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Quantity_and_Per_Unit_Amount_Not_Enterable" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>This boolean will make the Amount and Quantity not enterable on the expense report line.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Inactive" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Boolean flag indicating if the Expense Item is Inactive. Set for expense items that should no longer be selected on Expense Report Lines</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Hide_Itemization" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>True if you don't want to itemize the expense item on expense report lines.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Fixed_Expense" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Boolean flag indicating if the Expense Item is a Fixed Expense. Set for expenses that are always the same amount, for example, a fixed rate for mileage.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Maximum_Line_Expense" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Boolean flag indicating if the Expense Item has a Maximum Expense. Set for expenses where you want to establish a maximum amount that can't be exceeded, such as the maximum amount for one night at a hotel.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Maximum_Daily_Expense" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Boolean flag indicating if the Expense Item has a Maximum Daily Expense. Set for expenses where you want to establish a maximum daily amount that can't be exceeded, such as the maximum daily amount per meal.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Allow_Overage" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Boolean flag indicating if a Maximum Expense Item will allow overages. Set for expenses where you want to give the user a warning that they have surpassed the maximum amount allowed for the expense item rather than giving the user an error.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Based_on_Allowance_Plan" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Boolean flag indicating if the Expense Item is based on an Allowance Plan. Set for expenses that would have a Tuition Allowance Plan for example.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Memo_Required" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Boolean flag indicating if a Memo is Required by the user when entering the expense item.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Display_Arrival_Date_before_Departure_Date" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Display Arrival Date before Departure Date</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Non_Editable_Number_of_Days" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>This boolean will make the Number of Days not enterable on the expense report lines.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Expense_Item_Attribute_Data" type="wd:Expense_Item_Attribute_and_Type_Subedit_Web_ServiceType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>List of Expense Item Attributes</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Expense_Accumulator_Reference" type="wd:Expense_AccumulatorObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to an existing Expense Accumulator. This will determine if an accumulated quantity of all the expense report lines of the expense payee with this expense item will be evaluated by the base rate table. This should only be selected in conjunction with an Expense Rate Table.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Expense_Rate_Table_Reference" type="wd:Expense_Rate_TableObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to an existing Expense Rate Table. The Expense Rate Table is used to determine the base fixed or maximum amount of the Expense Item based on additional data entered by the user on the expense item details of an expense report line.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Enable_Rate_Tables_for_Spend_Authorizations" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Boolean flag, Enable Rate Tables on Spend Authorizations, that allows rate tables to be enforced on the spend authorization line using the expense item. This boolean will force all expense item attributes required by the related rate table to be displayed on required on spend authorizations. This boolean will only be available when a base rate table exists on the expense item.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Multiply_Per_Diem_by_Number_of_Days_on_Spend_Authorization" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
