</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Corporate_Payment_Responsibility_Reference" type="wd:Corporate_Payment_ResponsibilityObjectType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Corporate Payment Responsibility of this Corporate Credit Card Account. e.g. Corporate, Shared, Individual</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Expense_Item_Reference" type="wd:Expense_ItemObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Restrict usage of this Corporate Credit Card Account to specific Expense Items when filing an Expense Report with a Credit Card Transaction. Leave blank to allow any Expense Item to be used with this Corporate Credit Card Account on an Expense Report line.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Electronic_Load_Only" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>If left false, credit card transactions can be entered "manually" by users on Expense Report lines, by specifying the Credit Card on the Expense Report line.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Ensure Corporate Credit Card Accounts used for Procurement Credit Cards cannot be used to enter manual credit card transactions.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The electronic load only must be true when the usage is Procurement.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>To enable Pay Unapproved Expense Credit Card Transactions, you must also enable Electronic Load Only.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Electronic Load Only is required to enable Pay Unapproved Expense Card Transactions.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>To enable Use Company on Credit Card Account for Expense Accounting, you must also enable Electronic Load Only.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Electronic Load Only is required to enable Use Company on Credit Card Account for Expense Accounting.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Allow_Negative_Reimbursable_Total" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Whether or not the Reimbursable Total amount for the Corporate Credit Card Account can be negative on a given Expense Report.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Pay_Unapproved_Credit_Card_Transactions" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>When this flag is set to true, credit card transactions can be paid before being approved. This is only available for corporate credit card accounts used for Procurement.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Ensure the Pay Unapproved Credit Card Transactions flag is not set to true when the usage indicator is not Procurement.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Pay Unapproved Credit Card Transactions flag must be false or not present when the usage indicator is not Procurement.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Company_Reference" type="wd:CompanyObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The Company to be used for the Corporate Credit Card Account.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You are unable to change the company when the Corporate Credit Card Account already has transactions associated with it.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Spend_Category_Reference" type="wd:Spend_CategoryObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The Spend Category to be used for the Corporate Credit Card Account.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Balancing_Worktag_Reference" type="wd:Balancing_WorktagObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The Balancing Worktag to be used for the Corporate Credit Card Account.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Ensure the Balancing Worktag specified is used for Accounting purposes.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The balancing worktag must be of type: [type]</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>The worktag of the Corporate Credit Card Accounts can't be added or updated if Company doesn't have a Balancing Worktag configured.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You must first configure a balancing worktag for the Company to change or add a balancing worktag on the Corporate Credit Card Account.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>The worktag of a Corporate Credit Card Accounts cannot be changed if there are already associated Credit Card Transactions.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You are unable to change the Balancing worktag when the Corporate Credit Card Account already has transactions associated with it.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Optional_Balancing_Worktags_Reference" type="wd:Accounting_WorktagObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The Optional Balancing Worktags to be used for the Corporate Credit Card Account</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Ensure there is only one worktag of each type specified in the Optional Balancing Worktags.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Only one worktag of each type is allowed</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Ensure the Optional Balancing Worktags are enabled in the tenant.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Optional Balancing Worktags are not enabled on the tenant. Remove from the request and submit again.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Default_Worktag_Reference" type="wd:Audited_Accounting_WorktagObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Default Worktag</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>To add Default Worktags, you must first enable Pay Unapproved Expense Card Transactions.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>To add Default Worktags, you must enable Pay Unapproved Expense Card Transactions.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Duplicate worktag entries found. You can configure a worktag only once for either Balancing Worktags, Optional Worktags, or Default Worktags.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>A worktag can only be configured for 1 worktag configuration. Remove the duplicate worktag entry.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>[invalid worktag value message]</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Is_Inactive" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Read-Only; Returns true if corporate credit card account has been inactivated.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Only_pay_Transactions_from_Expense_Reports_already_paid_to_Worker" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Only pay transactions on Expense Reports already paid to worker</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Pay_Unapproved_Expense_Card_Transactions" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Pay Unapproved Expense Card Transactions</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>To enable Pay Unapproved Expense Card Transactions, you must configure the Payment Responsibility as Corporate.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>To enable Pay Unapproved Expense Card Transactions, the Payment Responsibility must be Corporate.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>To enable Pay Unapproved Expense Card Transactions, you must configure the Usage as Expenses.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>To enable Pay Unapproved Expense Card Transactions, the Usage must be Expenses.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't update this field if you have ongoing credit card transactions with these statuses: Expensed, Loading, New, and Pending.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Use_Company_on_Credit_Card_Account_for_Expense_Accounting" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Use Company on Credit Card Account for Expense Accounting</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>To enable Pay Unapproved Expense Card Transactions, you must first enable Use Company on Credit Card Account for Expense Accounting.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>To enable Pay Unapproved Expense Card Transactions, you must enable Use Company on Credit Card Account for Expense Accounting</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>To enable Pay Unapproved Expense Card Transactions, you must configure the Payment Responsibility as Corporate or Shared.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>To enable Use Company on Credit Card Account for Expense Accounting, the Payment Responsibility must be Corporate or Shared.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>To enable Pay Unapproved Expense Card Transactions, you must configure the Usage as Expenses.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>To enable Use Company on Credit Card Account for Expense Accounting, the Usage must be Expenses.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't update this field if you have ongoing credit card transactions with these statuses: Expensed, Loading, New, and Pending.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Self-service_Users_Can_t_Close_Transactions" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Whether or not self-service users can include these Credit Card Transactions on Expense Reports.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>To enable Pay Unapproved Expense Card Transactions, you must first enable Self-Service Users Can't Close Transactions.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>To enable Pay Unapproved Expense Card Transactions, you must enable Self-Service Users Can't Close Transactions.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Enable_Editing_on_the_Date_Field_on_Expense_Report_Lines_with_Credit_Card_Transactions" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Display a Receipt Date field on expense report lines with credit card transactions.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Payment_Type_Reference" type="wd:Payment_TypeObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Billing currency of the Corporate Credit Card Account to support internal reporting requirements.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Produce_Remittance_File" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Whether or not a Remittance File will be produced.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Market_Code" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Enter the financial institution provided market code to be used in the Workday generated remittance data.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Load_Number" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Enter the financial institution provided load number to be used in the Workday generated remittance data.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Country_Reference" type="wd:CountryObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Country visible in the Payment Details of the Corporate Credit Card Account.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Billing_Currency_Reference" type="wd:CurrencyObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Currency visible in the Payment Details of the Corporate Credit Card Account.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Integration_System_Reference" type="wd:Integration_System__Audited_ObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Remittance Integration System visible in the Payment Details of the Corporate Credit Card Account.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Contact_Data" type="wd:Contact_Information_DataType" minOccurs="0"/>
<xsd:element name="Settlement_Account_Data" type="wd:Settlement_Account_WWS_DataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
<xsd:element name="Alternate_Name_Data" type="wd:Business_Entity_Alternate_Name_DataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
<xsd:element name="Payment_Identifier" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Enter the financial institution provided payment identifier to be used in credit card payment files. For American Express, this value can be Load Number, Corporate Identifier (CID), Deposit ID or Book Number.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Expense_Credit_Card_DataType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Element containing all Expense Credit Card data</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>An Expense Credit Card Token cannot be submitted without a GL 1205 Card Holder Listing File Reference.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>This credit card has an invalid usage and is unavailable for reassignment.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>This credit card has an invalid payment responsibility and is unavailable for reassignment.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The corporate credit card account for credit card reference ID [credit card identifier] cannot be modified because there are credit card transactions associated with this credit card.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Credit Card Category can only be Central Travel Card if the Corporate Credit Card Account Usage is for Expenses, the Payment Responsibility is Corporate, and Electronic Load Only is set to True.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>The Cardholder Reference is required.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Cardholder Reference is required.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Cardholder for credit card reference ID [credit card identifier] cannot be modified because there are credit card transactions associated with this credit card.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Multiple people have the cardholder ID [cardholder ID] and an expense credit card already has the same corporate billing account number and last 4 digits.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Specify a valid Organization. The Organization you submitted is invalid for your request.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Expense_Credit_Card_ID" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Expense Credit Card ID. This is the Expense Credit Card unique identifier</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Corporate_Credit_Card_Account_Reference" type="wd:Corporate_Credit_Card_AccountObjectType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Corporate Credit Card Account Reference for the Expense Credit Card.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Credit_Card_Category_Reference" type="wd:Credit_Card_CategoryObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Central Travel Card boolean for Worker Credit Card</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:choice>
<xsd:element name="Cardholder_Reference" type="wd:Expense_PayeeObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Cardholder Reference for the Expense Credit Card. This will only be used in the iLOAD.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Cardholder_ID" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Cardholder ID for the Expense Credit Card. This will only be used by the Integrations Web Service for a standard card holder listing file where the reference to an Expense Payee in Workday is not available.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:choice>
<xsd:element name="Credit_Card_Organizations_Reference" type="wd:OrganizationObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Organizations for Central Travel Card</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Credit_Card_Description" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Expense Credit Card Description.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Last_4_Digits_of_Credit_Card_Number" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Expense Credit Card Number Last 4 Digits.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:string">
<xsd:maxLength value="4"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Credit_Card_Expiration_Date" type="xsd:date" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Expense Credit Card Expiration Date.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Monthly_Limit" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Expense Credit Card Monthly Limit.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="12"/>
<xsd:minInclusive value="0"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="0"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Transaction_Limit" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Expense Credit Card Transaction Limit.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="12"/>
<xsd:minInclusive value="0"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="0"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Billing_Currency_Reference" type="wd:CurrencyObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Billing Currency Reference for Expense Credit Card.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Common_Reference_ID_Type>Currency_ID</wd:Common_Reference_ID_Type>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Cash_Access_Allowed" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Cash Access Allowed boolean for Expense Credit Card</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Cancel_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Expense Credit Card Cancel Date</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>A Cancel date must be provided since the Credit Card Status is canceled.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Cardmember_Embossed_Name" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Expense Credit Card Cardmember Embossed Name.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Document_Status_Reference" type="wd:Document_StatusObjectType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Document Status Reference for Expense Credit Card. The statuses are Error (this can occur if the standard card holder listing file does not provide all needed data), Active, Canceled, Deleted, and Suspended.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Card_Holder_Listing_File_Reference" type="wd:Cardholder_Listing_FileObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Card Holder Listing File Reference for Expense Credit Card. This reference will only be provided by the Integrations Web Service and it will represent the standard card holder listing file.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Expense_Credit_Card_Token" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Expense Credit Card Token will only be set by the Integrations Web Service for PCI. This Token will be a unique identifier for each Expense Credit Card. It will be used to represent the Expense Credit Card Numbers. It will get generated by Integrations.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Alternate_Account_Identifier" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Configure this field if you use remittance files. Provide the alternate account identifier from your financial institution's incoming credit card file. Workday uses this value in the Get Payments web service response, ensuring that it's included in the remittance file that you send to your financial institution.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Reassignment_Enabled" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Manual Reassignment Allowed boolean for Expense Credit Card</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Supplier_Invoice_DataType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Element containing all Supplier Invoice data</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Please enter at least one invoice line.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Please enter at least one invoice line.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Supplier reference is for a supplier that can be used as a basic worktag only.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Supplier reference is for a supplier that can be used as a basic worktag only.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>External Document Links are currently not enabled.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>External Document Links are currently not enabled.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Supplier Invoice Prepaid and Prepaid Line boolean values cannot both be set. If header level flag is set to true, it will automatically mark all lines prepaid. Set Prepaid flag either in Header level for all lines or in line level for each individual line.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Define currency conversion rates between the invoice currency and the default currency on the header or line company before using the web service.</wd:Validation_Message>
