<xsd:documentation>Do not specify a withholding tax code when the company is configured to use a third-party tax service for withholding tax and you haven't specified values for Supplier Invoice Line Third Party Withholding Tax Rate Data. Workday will update this value with data provided by the third-party tax service.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Do not specify a withholding tax code when the company is configured to use a third-party tax service for withholding tax and you haven't specified values for Supplier Invoice Line Third Party Withholding Tax Rate Data. Workday will update this value with data provided by the third-party tax service.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Specify a third-party withholding tax code. You can't specify other withholding tax codes when you specify values for Supplier Invoice Line Third Party Withholding Tax Rate Data.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Specify a third-party withholding tax code. You can't specify other withholding tax codes when you specify values for Supplier Invoice Line Third Party Withholding Tax Rate Data.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Specify a third-party transaction tax code. You can't specify other transaction tax codes when you specify values for Supplier Invoice Line Third Party Tax Rate Data.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Specify a third-party transaction tax code. You can't specify other transaction tax codes when you specify values for Supplier Invoice Line Third Party Tax Rate Data.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Specify a third-party transaction tax code. This data is required when you specify values for Supplier Invoice Line Third Party Tax Rate Data for an invoice line.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Specify a third-party transaction tax code. This data is required when you specify values for Supplier Invoice Line Third Party Tax Rate Data for an invoice line.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Specify a unique transaction tax rate for the tax document line.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Specify a unique transaction tax rate for the tax document line.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>You can't specify a third-party withholding tax code when the company is not configured to use a third-party tax service for withholding tax.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't specify a third-party withholding tax code when the company is not configured to use a third-party tax service for withholding tax.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>You can't specify values for Supplier Invoice Line Third Party Withholding Tax Rate Data when the company is not configured to use a third-party tax service for withholding tax.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't specify values for Supplier Invoice Line Third Party Withholding Tax Rate Data when the company is not configured to use a third-party tax service for withholding tax.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>You can't specify a third-party transaction tax code when the company is not configured to use a third-party tax service.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't specify a third-party transaction tax code when the company is not configured to use a third-party tax service.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>You can't specify values for Supplier Invoice Line Third Party Tax Rate Data when the company is not configured to use a third-party tax service.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't specify values for Supplier Invoice Line Third Party Tax Rate Data when the company is not configured to use a third-party tax service.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>You can't specify values for Supplier Invoice Line Third Party Tax Rate Data or Supplier Invoice Line Third Party Withholding Tax Rate Data for this document type. Workday doesn't support third-party tax calculations for this document type.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't specify values for Supplier Invoice Line Third Party Tax Rate Data or Supplier Invoice Line Third Party Withholding Tax Rate Data for this document type. Workday doesn't support third-party tax calculations for this document type.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Do not specify a value for Inclusive of Tax Amount when Amount Inclusive of Tax is set as false.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't specify a value for Inclusive of Tax Amount for this document type.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Do not specify a transaction tax code or transaction tax applicability when the company is configured to use a third-party tax service and you haven't specified values for Supplier Invoice Line Third Party Tax Rate Data. Workday will update these values with data provided by the third-party tax service.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Do not specify a transaction tax code or transaction tax applicability when the company is configured to use a third-party tax service and you haven't specified values for Supplier Invoice Line Third Party Tax Rate Data. Workday will update these values with data provided by the third-party tax service.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Specify an active tax applicability.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Enter a quantity that is less than or equal to the original quantity on the supplier invoice line for purchase order type: [purchase order type].</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't reduce the quantity on a supplier invoice line tied to a consolidated requisition line for purchase order type: [purchase order type].</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't change the quantity for an invoice line associated with an inventory lot and serial transaction.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Supplier_Invoice_Line_ID" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Supplier Invoice Line Reference ID. This is the Supplier Invoice Line unique identifier</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Setting of Supplier Invoice Line Reference ID is not allowed for Recurring Supplier Invoices or Ad Hoc Payments.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Supplier Invoice Document for the referenced Supplier Invoice Line must be equal to the Supplier Invoice Document in this request</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Setting of Supplier Invoice Line Reference ID is not allowed for add-only service requests</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Line_Order" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Optional line order. If specified, lines will be sorted by this value when displayed and when invoice is printed.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Intercompany_Affiliate_Reference" type="wd:CompanyObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>This is the reference id value of the Company.If this is blank, Workday will default the company from the invoice header. If a value is provided that is different from the invoice header, workday validates that there is an appropriate intercompany relationship configured.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Common_Reference_ID_Type>Company_Reference_ID</wd:Common_Reference_ID_Type>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>[2] is not configured to allow intercompany transactions with [1]</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Purchase_Item_Reference" type="wd:Procurement_ItemObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to an existing Purchase Item or the Supplier's Default Purchase Item. Purchase items are goods and services that are purchased from suppliers</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Common_Reference_ID_Type>Catalog_Item_ID</wd:Common_Reference_ID_Type>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Only Purchase Item and Catalog Item can be referenced in a supplier invoice.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Purchase Item Reference entered can not be directly referenced in the transaction.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>A Web Item cannot be directly entered as a Purchase Item Reference. You can only refer to them indirectly by using Purchase Order Line Reference.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>A Web Item cannot be directly entered as a Purchase Item Reference. You can only refer to them indirectly by using Purchase Order Line Reference.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Item_Description" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>An optional description of the item, especially useful if only a Spend Category is selected for this line.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Purchase_Order_Line_Reference" type="wd:Purchase_Order_LineObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>An optional reference to an existing Purchase Order Line in the Workday system. This is used to link the Supplier Invoice Line with a Purchase Order Line. If the invoice line is for an external Purchase Order (not available within Workday), leave this blank.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The currency for the Supplier Invoice ([Currency]) must match the currency for the Purchase Order related to the Purchase Order Line specified: [PO Line].</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Purchase Order Line referenced is verified on a Procurement Card Transaction Verification report and can not be invoiced.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>The Purchase Order Line referenced is from a PO that is Closed or Pending Close.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Purchase Order Line referenced is from a PO that is Closed or Pending Close.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Supplier Contract specified for the Invoice does not match the Supplier Contract for the Purchase Order Line: [line].</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Supplier_Contract_Line_Reference" type="wd:Supplier_Contract_LineObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>An optional reference to an existing Supplier Contract Line in the Workday system. This is used to link the Supplier Invoice Line with a Supplier Contract Line. Is not allowed for Ad Hoc Requests, Supplier Contract Adjustments, or Supplier Invoice Contracts (Recurring Supplier Invoices).</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The currency for the Supplier Invoice ([Currency]) must match the currency ([Contract Line Currency]) for the Supplier Contract Line specified: [Contract Line].</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Spend Category ([inv line spend category]) on the Invoice Line does not match the Spend Category ([supp contract line spend category])on the Supplier Contract Line.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Supplier Contract specified for the Invoice Line does not match the Supplier Contract for the Supplier Contract Line: [line].</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Customer_Invoice_Line_Reference" type="wd:Customer_Invoice_LineObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>An optional reference to an existing Customer Invoice Line in the Workday system. This is used to link the Supplier Invoice Line with a Customer Invoice for Direct Intercompany Invoices.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The currency for the Supplier Invoice ([Currency]) must match the currency for the Customer Invoice related to the Customer Invoice Line specified: [Customer Invoice Line].</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't enter a discount override date or discount override amount for a direct intercompany invoice.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Supplier_Invoice_Line_to_Adjust_Reference" type="wd:Supplier_Invoice_Line_AbstractObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The Supplier Invoice Line to Adjust Reference for the adjustment must be for the same company, must be approved, amounts must be valid, and the asset cannot have events in progress. The reference must be to a supplier invoice line.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Spend_Category_Reference" type="wd:Spend_CategoryObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to an existing Spend Category</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Commodity_Code_Reference" type="wd:Commodity_CodeObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A reference to the Commodity Code for the invoice line. You can add WID or Reference ID to populate this field. If the Invoice originates or references (for creating or adjusting supplier invoices respectively) a related purchase order, it populates the value from the purchase order and is read-only.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Ship_To_Address_Reference" type="wd:Address_ReferenceObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Contains a reference instance or a Address Reference ID for an existing address</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Ship_To_Contact_Reference" type="wd:WorkerObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to a Worker, who will be the designated Ship-To Contact.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Ship-From_Address_Reference" type="wd:Address_ReferenceObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to an existing Ship-From address.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Setting of Invoice Line Ship-From Address is not allowed for Recurring Supplier Invoices or Ad-hoc Payment.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The address [address] is invalid for the supplier: [supplier]. Use the supplier change configuration to add a valid shipping address for this supplier.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Accounting_Treatment_Reference" type="wd:Accounting_TreatmentObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>This is the accounting treatment of a trackable item line derived from business asset accounting rules.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Trackable_Item" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>This is the track items attribute on Spend Category, at the time the supplier invoice was submitted. As spend categories can change over time, this value is persisted for reporting purposes.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Tax_Applicability_Reference" type="wd:Tax_ApplicabilityObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>This is the reference id value of the tax applicability.If this is blank and there invoice line has a sales item, Workday will default tax applicability from the sales item. If the invoice line has a tax code then tax applicability is required.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Tax Applicability Reference is required if Tax Code Reference is provided.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Tax Applicability Reference is required if Tax Code Reference is provided.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Tax_Code_Reference" type="wd:Tax_CodeObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>This is the reference id value of the tax code.If this is blank, Workday will default in the default tax code from the invoice header if there is one. If the invoice line has a tax applicability value, Workday will validate that the invoice line also has a tax code.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Tax Code on the line is only allowed if the Tax Option is Calculate Tax Due to Supplier or Calculate Use Tax.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>A Tax Code should be entered on a Tax Only Invoice when Calculate Tax Due to Supplier or Calculate Self Assessed Tax tax options are selected.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>A Tax Code should be entered on a Tax Only Invoice when Calculate Tax Due to Supplier or Calculate Self Assessed Tax tax options are selected.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Withholding_Tax_Code_Reference" type="wd:Tax_CodeObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>This is the reference id value of the withholding tax code.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Select a withholding tax code that does not have a realization point of Customer Invoice Self Withholding.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Tax_Data" type="wd:Tax_Widget_DataType" minOccurs="0"/>
<xsd:element name="Tax_Rate_Options_Data" type="wd:Tax_Rate_Options_DataType" minOccurs="0"/>
<xsd:element name="Packaging_String" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Packaging String associated with the Item specified on the Supplier Invoice or Adjustment Line. This is not applicable to Ad Hoc payment lines.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Quantity" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>If this is blank, Workday will assume a value of 1. If invoice line has a quantity and unit price, then Workday will automatically calculate extended amount. But if the line references either a Service or Project-Based Purchase Order or Contract Line, the quantity must be blank and extended amount will not be calculated.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Splitting by quantity is not allowed when the quantity is not a whole number: [qty]</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Split by Quantity is not allowed for lines referencing Service or Project-Based Supplier Contract Lines.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Quantity cannot be set for lines referencing Service or Project-Based Supplier Contract Lines.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Unit cost and/or Quantity cannot be negative for inventory items from a purchase order line</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="22"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="2"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Unit_of_Measure_Reference" type="wd:Unit_of_MeasureObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Unit of Measure for the Supplier Invoice Line to be created or modified.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Invalid unit of measure ([Unit Of Measure]) for purchase item ([Purchase Item]). Unit of measure must be the same as the source document line ([Source Document Line]).</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Invalid unit of measure for catalog item. Unit of measure is not a defined ordering unit of measure or is not the same as the source document line unit of measure.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Invalid unit of measure ([Unit Of Measure]) for catalog item ([Catalog Item]). Unit of measure must be the same as the source document line ([Source Document Line]).</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Select a unit of measure that is already in use for the supplier item.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Select the unit of measure already in use on the original document line.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Unit_Cost" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>This is the Unit Price. If this is blank, Workday will default the unit price from the item if one is configured. If invoice line has a quantity and unit price, then Workday will automatically calculate extended amount.. But if the line references either a Service or Project-Based Purchase Order or Contract Line, the Unit Price must be blank.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Unit Cost cannot be set for lines referencing Service or Project-Based Supplier Contract or Purchase Order Lines.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Unit cost and/or Quantity cannot be negative for inventory items from a purchase order line</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Extended_Amount" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>This is the invoice line amount. If the invoice line has a quantity and unit price, then Workday will automatically calculate extended amount.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Please enter an extended amount</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="18"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="3"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Inclusive_of_Tax_Amount" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The total amount of the invoice line, including tax. This value is used in conjunction with Amount Inclusive of Tax to enable third-party tax calculations from an amount that includes tax. If you set Amount Inclusive of Tax as true, Workday will populate this value after a third-party tax service calculates taxes. When you're submitting third-party tax rate data, set Amount Inclusive of Tax as true and specify a value for Inclusive of Tax Amount.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="18"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="3"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Retention_Amount" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The amount to retain from this invoice line.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Retention Amount is only allowed if the Supplier Invoice line is related to a PO/Contract line that is subject to retention</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Retention Amount can not be more than Extended Amount</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="18"/>
<xsd:minInclusive value="0"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="3"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Payment_Amount" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The Payment Amount is equal to the extended amount minus the retention amount. This field only returns values.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="18"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="3"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Budget_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Use this field to override the Budget Date from the supplier invoice header.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Prepaid" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Prepaid flag at the Line level</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Your spend category for this line is not eligible for Prepaid.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>The Prepaid flag cannot be checked for a Tax Only Invoice Type.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Prepaid flag cannot be checked for a Tax Only Invoice Type.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Supplier_Contract_Reference" type="wd:Supplier_ContractObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>This field is only enabled for Companies and Tenants which are Opted-In to Consolidate Requisition Lines by Supplier regardless of Supplier Contract.Use this field to assign a specific Supplier Contract to this Spend Line.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Supplier Contract ([supplier contract]) on the Supplier Invoice Line cannot be used because it is referenced on a Procurement Card Verification.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Supplier Contract selected on the Document Line must be for the Supplier on the Document Header.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Supplier Contract field on the Invoice line is required if there is a Contract Line referenced.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Original Supplier Invoice was created from a schedule. The Adjustment's Contract ([adjustment contract]) is required to be the same as the original Supplier Invoice Contract ([orig contract]).</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>The Supplier Contract selected must be for the Supplier on the invoice.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Supplier Contract selected must be for the Supplier on the invoice.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>The Supplier Contract on the Document Line is Closed or Pending Close.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Supplier Contract on the Document Line is Closed or Pending Close.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>You selected an invalid supplier contract for this supplier invoice line. Select a supplier contract that's valid for the company, supplier, and document date; not undergoing an amendment; and supports manual supplier invoices.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You selected an invalid supplier contract for this supplier invoice line. Select a supplier contract that's valid for the company, supplier, and document date; not undergoing an amendment; and supports manual supplier invoices.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Invoice_Line_Delivery_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Enter Invoice Line Delivery Date</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Setting of Invoice Line Delivery Date is not allowed for Recurring Supplier Invoices or Ad Hoc Payments.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Invoice_Line_Billing_Start_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Enter Invoice Line Billing Start Date</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Setting of Invoice Line Billing Start Date is not allowed for Recurring Supplier Invoices or Ad Hoc Payments.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Invoice_Line_Billing_End_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Enter Invoice Line Billing End Date</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Invoice Line Billing End Date must be greater than or equal to the Invoice Line Billing Start Date.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Setting of Invoice Line Billing End Date is not allowed for Recurring Supplier Invoices or Ad Hoc Payments.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Memo" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Memo for the Invoice line. This is free form text.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Worktags_Reference" type="wd:Accounting_WorktagObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to existing worktags. Worktags are a way to mark tasks and business objects to make them easier to access and summarize. Each transaction can include one value for each worktag type and is subject to configurable validation when submitted for approval.</xsd:documentation>
