<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Select just 1 worktag for each type on each document line.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Only one worktag for each type is allowed for each document line.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Specify a percentage between 0 and 100.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Percentage entered must be between 0 to 100%.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Specify a value in the worktag balancing field only if worktag balancing is configured and the project is a capital project.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Worktag balancing field may only be entered if worktag balancing is configured and the project is a Capital Project.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Added a validation to check that the Optional Balancing Worktag can only be entered for a capital project template if the tenant is configured for optional balancing worktags.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The project must be a capital project since optional balancing worktags are included and the tenant is configured for optional balancing worktags.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Added validation to check that the Optional Balancing Worktag types are among the allowed Worktag Types specified by the Maintain Worktag Balancing Configuration task.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Optional Balancing Worktag field must meet the type requirements specified on the Maintain Worktag Balancing Configuration task.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Added validation to check that a project template cannot have 2 Optional Balancing Worktags of the same Worktag Type.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Optional Balancing Worktags cannot contain 2 worktags of the same type.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Added new validation to prevent entries to fields other than Default Worktags.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Remove references to all fields except Default Worktags. Workday only supports default worktags for this web service.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Added a new validation to recommend that workers should remove the reference to a worktag to delete it instead of selecting the Delete option.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Remove the reference to the worktag you want to delete instead of selecting the Delete option in your web service request. If you submit a request with no worktags, Workday removes references to all existing worktags automatically.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Added validation to check that a project template cannot be marked with an optional balancing worktag of type Project.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>A project template cannot be marked with an optional balancing worktag of type Project.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Added validation to require the user to specify a value for Optional Balancing Worktags that were set as Default Required.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You must specify a value for required worktag(s): [required optional worktags]</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Added Validation to check the optional balancing worktags are valid to use with the company.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The [type] is/are not available for use with the company/s: [partitionable] [company]</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Added Validation to check the balancing worktag is valid to use with the company.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The [type] is/are not available for use with the company/s: [partitionable] [company]</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Confirms that the default related worktags are valid for use with the company.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>[concatenated validation message for constraint provider for Put Project Template]</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>This validation prevents entering a customer contract template without project lines.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Specify a customer contract template that is eligible for projects.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
