<xsd:documentation>You must enter a Quantity when Line Split Allocation Reference is Split by Quantity.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You must enter a Quantity when Line Split Allocation Reference is Split by Quantity.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Quantity must be empty when Line Split Allocation Reference is Split by Amount.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Quantity must be empty when Line Split Allocation Reference is Split by Amount.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="22"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="2"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Extended_Amount" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The extended amount for the split line. This is always required and must be correct (quantity * unit cost of parent line).</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="18"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="3"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Memo" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Memo for the Split line. This is free form text.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Line_Split_Allocation_Reference" type="wd:Business_Document_Line_SplitObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to an existing Purchase Order line split or Supplier Invoice Line Split to Adjust</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Budget_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Use this field to override the Budget Date from the supplier invoice header.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Worktag_Reference" type="wd:Accounting_WorktagObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to existing worktags. Worktags are a way to mark tasks and business objects to make them easier to access and summarize.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>[list of worktag types] not valid for this transaction.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>You have chosen an invalid combination of header company, line company, and intercompany affiliate.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The intercompany affiliate [worktag] may not be chosen when specifying header company [header company] and line company [line company].</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>For supplier invoice line splits tagged with a capital project worktag, the company of the invoice line split must equal the company on the capital project.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>For supplier invoice line splits tagged with a capital project worktag, the company of the invoice line split must equal the company on the capital project.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Enter a company that matches on the award line in effect for grant: [grant]. This company doesn't match the grant on the award line: [comp].</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Transactions for contingent workers cannot have contingent worker worktags on line splits. Please remove the contingent worker worktag.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>[not allowed worktag types on Spend Transactions]</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The [type] is/are not available for use with the company/s: [partitionable] [company]</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>[worktag value] is not permitted as an allowed value for worktag type: [worktag type], because it is inactive.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Select a balancing worktag for Worktags of the following type: [type]</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The following Accounting Worktags are required but have not been assigned: [missing].</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>[missing required worktag types on Spend Transactions]</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>[invalid worktag value message]</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Billable" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Billable Flag at Invoice Line Split Level</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>The supplier invoice line split can't be marked as Billable if the selected Worktag is not for a billable project</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The supplier invoice line split can't be marked as Billable if the selected Worktag is not for a project plan,phase, or task from a billable project</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can mark a supplier invoice line split as Billable only for Supplier Invoices and Supplier Invoice Adjustments</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Clear the prepaid or billable option for the line when Deferred Project Cost Accounting is configured. Only 1 of these options can apply to the supplier invoice line split.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Clear the prepaid or billable option for the line when Deferred Project Cost Accounting is configured. Only 1 of these options can apply to the supplier invoice line split.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can’t set a supplier invoice line as billable and add an item or spend category with asset tracking. Either clear the Billable check box on the supplier invoice line or remove these items or spend categories: [items].</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can’t set a supplier invoice line as billable and add an item or spend category with asset tracking. Either clear the Billable check box on the supplier invoice line or remove these items or spend categories: [items].</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can’t set a supplier invoice line as billable and add an item or spend category with inventory tracking. Either clear the Billable check box on the supplier invoice line or remove these items or spend categories: [items].</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can’t set a supplier invoice line as billable and add an item or spend category with inventory tracking. Either clear the Billable check box on the supplier invoice line or remove these items or spend categories: [items].</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can’t set transactions as billable and add billable capital project worktags. Clear the Billable check box on the transaction lines or remove these worktags: [worktags].</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can’t set transactions as billable and add billable capital project worktags. Clear the Billable check box on the transaction lines or remove these worktags: [worktags].</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Transfer_Asset_To_Different_Company_DataType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Element containing data needed to transfer Asset to another Company.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Assets may not be transfered when it is of "Disposed" status.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Cannot transfer Capital Assets whose accounting has not been assigned.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Ledger period for transfer depreciation start date must exist for the companies that asset is getting transferred from and getting transferred to</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Ledger period for transfer depreciation start date must exist for the companies that asset is getting transferred from and getting transferred to</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Transfer date cannot be prior to last issue date, last transfer date or acquisition date, and cannot be after today</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Asset has a pending event that need be completed before transfer.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Transfer to Company must be an Intercompany Affiliate of the Originating Company of the asset.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Originating and transfer to companies must have matching default currencies.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Originating company and transfer to company cannot be the same.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Assets may not be transferred when it is of "Pending Registration" status.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The fiscal Period for the transaction date must exist in the fiscal schedule of every company asset book where this is a depreciable asset in order to do this transaction</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You cannot transfer an asset to a different company when asset status is Out of Service and the asset is getting transferred with cost as original. Asset depreciation has to be resumed before the asset can be transferred.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Assets may not be transferred when it is of 'Removed' status</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Transfer to Different Company is not allowed for Component Asset or Discrete Composite Asset.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't transfer this asset because the Company Asset Book Restrictions that are configured; the asset books no longer match the transfer to company. The fiscal schedule for each company asset book in the transfer from company must match the fiscal schedule for the same asset book in the transfer to company.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't transfer this asset because the asset books no longer match the transfer to company.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Specify a Transfer To Company whose asset books currencies match the currencies of the Transfer From Company.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Reference" type="wd:Business_AssetObjectType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Asset one would like to be transferred to another Company.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Common_Reference_ID_Type>Asset_ID</wd:Common_Reference_ID_Type>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>An Asset from Supplier Contract cannot be transferred to a different company.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Transaction_Effective_Date" type="xsd:date" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Transaction effective date of the asset transfer.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Transaction effective date of this transaction cannot be prior to last reclassification date for asset</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Transaction effective date of this transaction cannot be prior to last partial disposal date for asset</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Transfer_To_Company_Reference" type="wd:CompanyObjectType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Company one would like the Asset transferred to.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Common_Reference_ID_Type>Company_Reference_ID</wd:Common_Reference_ID_Type>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Transfer_Asset_To_Different_Company_RequestType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Element containing data needed to transfer Asset to another Company.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Business_Process_Parameters" type="wd:Financials_Business_Process_ParametersType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Business Process Parameters provide the ability to auto-submit to the business process.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Transfer_Asset_To_Different_Company_Data" type="wd:Transfer_Asset_To_Different_Company_DataType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Contains the items needed to Transfer an Asset to another Company.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
<xsd:attribute ref="wd:version"/>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Transfer_Asset_To_Different_Company_ResponseType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Returns Business Asset transferred to a different company.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Reference" type="wd:Business_AssetObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Returns Business Asset transferred to a different company.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Common_Reference_ID_Type>Asset_ID</wd:Common_Reference_ID_Type>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
<xsd:attribute ref="wd:version"/>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Asset_Request_ReferencesType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Nature of Actions Secondary Request Reference Element</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Reference" type="wd:Business_AssetObjectType" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>References to existing Assets to return data for in the response.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Asset_Request_CriteriaType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The Request Criteria is a wrapper element around a list of elements representing the operation specific criteria needed to search for assets.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>At least one field must be populated in order to search.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Company_Reference" type="wd:CompanyObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>One or more Company references to use to filter the assets returned in the response.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Issued_To_Worker_Reference" type="wd:WorkerObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>One or more Worker references to use to find assets currently issues to those Workers.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Spend_Category_Reference" type="wd:Spend_CategoryObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>One or more Spend Categories to find assets belonging to those categories.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Item_Reference" type="wd:Purchase_ItemObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>One or more Purchase Item references to find assets related to those items.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Location_Reference" type="wd:LocationObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>One or more Locations to find assets currently placed in those locations.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Identifier" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>An Asset Identifier value to be used to find any exsisting assets with the matching Asset Identifier value.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Serial_Number" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A value to be used to find any existing assets with a matching Serial Number value</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Worktag_Reference" type="wd:Accounting_WorktagObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>One or more Worktag references to be used to find Assets currently assigned any of these worktags. To filter based on Location, use the Location Reference element.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Status_Reference" type="wd:Document_StatusObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>One or more Asset Status reference to use to find assets currently in those statuses.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Acquisition_Method_Reference" type="wd:Acquisition_MethodObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>One or more Acquisition Method references to use to find assets acquired using one of those methods.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Disposal_Method_Reference" type="wd:Business_Asset_Disposal_MethodObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>One or more Asset Disposal Method references to find assets disposed of using those methods.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Acquired_From_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Allows you to find assets by the date they were acquired. This is the From Date to find assets by acquisition date. This date is inclusive.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>If Acquisition From Date or To Date is provided, the other must be provided also.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Acquired_To_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Allows you to find assets by the date they were acquired. This is the To Date to find assets by acquisition date. This date is inclusive.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Updated_From_Date" type="xsd:dateTime" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Allows you to find assets by when they were updated. This is the From Date to use to find all types of asset activity within a date range (Acquisition, Cost Adjustment, Disposal, Reinstatement, Issue, Transfer). Assets with activity in this date range will be returned in the response.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>If either Updated From Date or To Date is provided, the other must be provided also.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Updated_To_Date" type="xsd:dateTime" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Allows you to find assets by when they were updated. This is the To Date to use to find all types of asset activity within a date range (Acquisition, Cost Adjustment, Disposal, Reinstatement, Issue, Transfer). Assets with activity in this date range will be returned in the response.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Asset_Response_GroupType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The Response Group is a wrapper element around a list of elements representing the amount of data that should be included in the response.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Include_Reference" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>If true, a reference to the primary business object will be returned in the Get Response.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Include_Custodian_Data" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>If true, includes the Custodian Data element in the response.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Include_Depreciation_Data" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>If true, includes the Depreciation Data element in the response.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Include_Depreciation_Detail_Data" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>If true, includes the Depreciation Detail Data element in the response.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Include_Disposal_Data" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>If true, includes the Disposal Data element in the response.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Include_Intercompany_Transfer_Data" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>If true, includes the Intercompany Transfer Data element in the response.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Include_Impairment_Data" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>If true, includes the Impairment Data element in the response.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Include_Reinstatement_Data" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>If true, includes the Reinstatement Data element in the response.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Include_In_Service_Schedule_Data" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>If true, includes the In Service Schedule Data element in the response.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Include_Cost_Adjustment_Data" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>If true, includes the Cost Adjustment Data element in the response.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Include_Attachment_Data" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>If true, includes the Attachment Data element in the response.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Include_Reclassification_Data" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>If true, includes the Reclassification Data element in the response.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Include_Removal_Data" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>If true, includes the Removal Data element in the response.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Get_Assets_RequestType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Root element for the Request on the Get operation. Contains references, criteria, filter and response group for specifying which instances to return in the Response.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:choice>
<xsd:element name="Request_References" type="wd:Asset_Request_ReferencesType" minOccurs="0"/>
<xsd:element name="Request_Criteria" type="wd:Asset_Request_CriteriaType" minOccurs="0"/>
</xsd:choice>
<xsd:element name="Response_Filter" type="wd:Response_FilterType" minOccurs="0"/>
<xsd:element name="Response_Group" type="wd:Asset_Response_GroupType" minOccurs="0"/>
</xsd:sequence>
<xsd:attribute ref="wd:version"/>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="AssetType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Encapsulates a single Asset object, including a reference to the Asset, and all related data and transactions.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Reference" type="wd:Business_AssetObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A reference to the asset.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Data" type="wd:Asset_DataType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Encapsulates all the data for a single Asset.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Asset_Response_DataType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Contains all the Assets returned by the web service operation.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Asset" type="wd:AssetType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Get_Assets_ResponseType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>This element is the top-level response element for all Get Assets operations</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Request_References" type="wd:Asset_Request_ReferencesType" minOccurs="0"/>
<xsd:element name="Request_Criteria" type="wd:Asset_Request_CriteriaType" minOccurs="0"/>
<xsd:element name="Response_Filter" type="wd:Response_FilterType" minOccurs="0"/>
<xsd:element name="Response_Group" type="wd:Asset_Response_GroupType" minOccurs="0"/>
<xsd:element name="Response_Results" type="wd:Response_ResultsType" minOccurs="0"/>
<xsd:element name="Response_Data" type="wd:Asset_Response_DataType" minOccurs="0"/>
</xsd:sequence>
<xsd:attribute ref="wd:version"/>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Asset_DataType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Encapsulates all the data for a single Asset.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Reference_ID" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A unique identifier for the Asset.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Asset_ID" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The primary ID of this asset. This is a unique ID that can be used to identify this asset instance.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Company_Reference" type="wd:CompanyObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A reference to the Company this asset belongs to.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Currency_Reference" type="wd:CurrencyObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The base currency for the company this asset belongs to.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Name" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The name of the asset.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Description" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A text description of the asset.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Status_Reference" type="wd:Document_StatusObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A reference to the current status of the asset.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Spend_Category_Reference" type="wd:Spend_CategoryObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A reference to the Spend Category this asset belongs to.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Total_Asset_Cost" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The current total cost of this asset.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Quantity" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The number of units</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="12"/>
<xsd:minInclusive value="0"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="0"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Quantity_Available" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Units available</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="12"/>
<xsd:minInclusive value="0"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="0"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Residual_Value" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The current residual value of this asset.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Date_Placed_In_Service" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The date this asset was placed in service.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Accounting_Treatment_Reference" type="wd:Accounting_TreatmentObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A reference to the Accounting Treatment used for this asset.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Identifier" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The asset identifier for this asset.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Serial_Number" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The serial number assigned to this asset.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Manufacturer" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The manufacturer for the Asset, as a text value.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Class_Reference" type="wd:Asset_ClassObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A reference to the Asset Class for this asset.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Type_Reference" type="wd:Asset_TypeObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A reference to the Asset Type for this asset.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Business_Use_Percentage" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The Business Use Percentage for this asset, as a number from 1 to 100.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="12"/>
<xsd:minInclusive value="0"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="0"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Coordinating_Cost_Center_Reference" type="wd:Cost_CenterObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>References the coordinating cost center for reporting only.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Coordinator_Reference" type="wd:WorkerObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>References the asset coordinator for reporting only.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Related_Asset_Reference" type="wd:Business_AssetObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A reference to other assets that are related to this one.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Event_In_Progress" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A boolean returning True if the asset has an event in progress.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Share_Reference" type="wd:Asset_Share_Response_DataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
<xsd:element name="Acquisition_Data" type="wd:Asset_Acquisition_WWS_DataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
<xsd:element name="Custodian_Data" type="wd:Asset_Custodian_WWS_DataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Component_Data" type="wd:Asset_Components_WWS_DataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
<xsd:element name="Depreciation_Data" type="wd:Asset_Depreciation_WWS_DataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
<xsd:element name="Disposal_Data" type="wd:Asset_Disposal_WWS_DataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
<xsd:element name="Depreciation_Detail_Data" type="wd:Asset_Depreciation_Detail_DataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
<xsd:element name="Reinstatement_Data" type="wd:Asset_Reinstatement_WWS_DataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
<xsd:element name="Intercompany_Transfer_Data" type="wd:Asset_Intercompany_Transfer_WWS_DataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
<xsd:element name="Impairment_Data" type="wd:Asset_Impairment_WWS_DataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
<xsd:element name="In_Service_Schedule_Data" type="wd:Asset_In_Service_Schedule_WWS_DataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
<xsd:element name="Cost_Adjustment_Data" type="wd:Asset_Cost_Adjustment_WWS_DataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
<xsd:element name="Reclassification_Data" type="wd:Asset_Reclassification_WWS_DataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
<xsd:element name="Removal_Data" type="wd:Asset_Removal_WWS_DataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
<xsd:element name="Attachment_Data" type="wd:Financials_Attachment_DataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="CC_Transaction_LineType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Credit Card Transaction Line Data</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Credit_Card_Transaction_Line_ID" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Credit Card Transaction Line ID.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="12"/>
<xsd:minInclusive value="0"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="0"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Purchase_Order_Line_Number" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The line number of the Purchase Order.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="4"/>
<xsd:minInclusive value="0"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="0"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Item_Description" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Item Description</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="UNSPSC_code" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>UNSPSC Code</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="12"/>
<xsd:minInclusive value="0"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="0"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="UPC" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Universal Product Code</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Vendor_Part_Number" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Vendor Part Number</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Quantity" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Quantity</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="22"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="2"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Unit_of_Measure_Reference" type="wd:Unit_of_MeasureObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to an existing Unit of Measure</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Unit_Price" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Item Unit Price</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Extended_Amount" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Extended Amount</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="18"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="3"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Tax_Rate" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to Line Tax Rate</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="15"/>
<xsd:minInclusive value="0"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="12"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Tax_Amount" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Total Tax Amount for Tax Rate</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Freight_Amount" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Freight charges incurred.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Handling_Amount" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Handling charges incurred.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Discount_Amount" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Amount of discount applied.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Flat_Rate_Amount" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Flat rate negotiated.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Lost_or_Damaged_Items_Amount" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Charges as a result of lost or damaged items.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="One_Time_Miscellaneous_Charges_Amount" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>One time only charges.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Other_Charges_Amount" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Other miscellaneous charges.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Miscellaneous_Charges_Amount" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Sum of all other charges submitted.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Miscellaneous_Charges_Description" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Description of Miscellaneous Charges Amount.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Item_Code_Description" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Description of the individual Item purchased</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Charge_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Date of individual Purchase Transaction.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Line_Item_Total_Amount" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Sum of a line Item net of discounts in original currency</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="18"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="4"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Product_Code" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Product Code of the individual Item purchased.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Item_Sequence_Number" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Sequence number of an item in a Lodging/car rental detail transaction. Sequentially increased value to differentiate successive records.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="10"/>
<xsd:minInclusive value="0"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="0"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Asset_Acquisition_WWS_DataType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Contains data related to the acquisition or creation of the asset. This includes the date, method, initial cost, and source information.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Acquisition_Cost" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The initial cost when the asset was acquired.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Acquisition_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The date the asset was acquired, or the transaction effective date of the acquisition.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Acquisition_Method_Reference" type="wd:Acquisition_MethodObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A reference to the Acquisition Method this asset was acquired with.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="PO_Number" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>If this asset was created from a Purchase order, this is the PO Number for that Purchase Order.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Receipt_Number" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>If this asset was created from a Receipt, this is the Receipt number the asset was created from.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Supplier_Invoice_Number" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>If this asset was created from a Supplier Invoice, this is the Supplier Invoice Number the asset was created from.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Residual_Value_At_Acquisition" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The residual value at the time of acquisition.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Supplier_Invoice_Line_Reference" type="wd:Supplier_Invoice_Line_AbstractObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>If this asset was created from a Supplier Invoice, this is a reference to the corresponding Supplier Invoice Line.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Receipt_Line_Reference" type="wd:Unique_IdentifierObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>If this asset was created from a Receipt, this is a reference to the corresponding Receipt Line.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Transfer_From_Business_Asset_Reference" type="wd:Business_AssetObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>If this asset was created as the result of transfer an existing asset to different company, this is the original source asset that was transferred to create this one.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Worktag_Reference" type="wd:Audited_Accounting_WorktagObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The worktags specified on the initial acquisition transaction.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Memo" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Memo from manual registration.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Project_Number" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Project number for the business asset.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="External_Contract_Number" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>External Contract Number from manual registration.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Lease_Accounting_Method_Reference" type="wd:Lease_Accounting_MethodObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Lease Accounting Method for Leased Asset from Supplier Contract.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Supplier_Contract_Type_Reference" type="wd:Supplier_Contract_TypeObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Supplier Contract Type for Leased Asset from Supplier Contract.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="External_Contract_Start_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>External Contract Start Date from manual registration.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="External_Contract_End_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>External Contract End Date from manual registration.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Alternate_Merchant_Name_DataType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Alternate Names for Merchant are entered here.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Cannot have duplicate alternate names.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>[alternate_name] is already used as an alternate name.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>[alternate_name] is already used a merchant name.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Alternate_Name_Value" type="xsd:string" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Alternate Name Value</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Asset_In_Service_Schedule_WWS_DataType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Contains data the in-service schedule for this asset. This is present for each period of time the asset is in service, and can occur repeatedly if the asset is suspended, and later resumed.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="In_Service_From_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The start date for the in-service period for this asset.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="In_Service_To_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The end date for the in-service period for this asset.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Asset_Impairment_WWS_DataType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Contains data for impairment activity for this asset.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Transaction_Effective_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The date the asset was impaired or the transaction effective date of the impairment.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Current_Fair_Market_Value" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The current fair market value at the time of the impairment.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Revised_Fair_Market_Value" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The revised fair market value after the impairment was recorded.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Impairment_Amount" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The impairment amount. This is the difference between the Current Fair Market Value and Revised Fair Market Value for the asset impairment.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Impairment_Reason_Reference" type="wd:Asset_Impairment_ReasonObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A reference to the reason recorded for the asset impairment.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Comment" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Comments entered by the user when impairing the asset.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Asset_Intercompany_Transfer_WWS_DataType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Contains information about transfers to or from a different company for this asset.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Transaction_Effective_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The date the asset was transferred from or to a different company (the transaction effective date of the transfer).</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Transfer_To_Company_Reference" type="wd:CompanyObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>If this asset was transferred to a different company, this is a reference to that company.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Transfer_From_Company_Reference" type="wd:CompanyObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>If this asset was transferred FROM a different company, this is a reference to that company.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Accumulated_Depreciation" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The accumulated depreciation amount at the time the asset was transferred to a different company.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Transfer_To_Asset_Reference" type="wd:Business_AssetObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A reference to the new Asset that was created as a result of transferring this Asset to a different Company.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Asset_Reinstatement_WWS_DataType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Contains information about reinstatement activity for this asset.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Transaction_Effective_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The date the asset was reinstated (the transaction effective date of the reinstatement).</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Disposal_Type_Reference" type="wd:Asset_Disposal_TypeObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The Disposal Type for the Disposal transaction that this Reinstatement is linked to.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Disposal_Fair_Market_Value" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The Disposal Fair Market Value for the Disposal transaction that this Reinstatement is linked to.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Sale_Price" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The Disposal Sale Price for the Disposal transaction that this Reinstatement is linked to.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Comment" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Comments entered by the user when reinstating the asset.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Worktag_Reference" type="wd:Audited_Accounting_WorktagObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The Worktags for the Disposal transaction that this Reinstatement is linked to.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Asset_Disposal_WWS_DataType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Contains data for each time an asset was disposed. An asset may have more than one disposal activity if it was reinstated after a prior disposal.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Transaction_Effective_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The date the asset was disposed or the transaction effective date of the disposal.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Disposal_Cost" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The cost that was disposed.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Disposal_Percent" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The percent of cost at time of disposal that was disposed. If percent is not 100, disposal is considered partial.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="19"/>
<xsd:minInclusive value="0"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="16"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Disposal_Type_Reference" type="wd:Asset_Disposal_TypeObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A reference to the type of disposal</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Disposal_Fair_Market_Value" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The fair market value of the asset at the time it was disposed.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Sale_Price" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The sale price, if the asset was sold as part of the disposal activity.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Net_Book_Value_at_Disposal" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The net book value of the asset at the time it was disposed.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Disposal_Gain" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The amount gained at disposal versus the asset's cost.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Disposal_Loss" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The amount lost at disposal versus the asset's cost.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Donation_Amount" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The value of the donation of the asset, if applicable.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Comment" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Comments entered by the user when disposing the asset.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Disposal_Worktags_Reference" type="wd:Accounting_WorktagObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The worktags associated with the asset disposal activity.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Asset_Depreciation_WWS_DataType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Contains information about this asset related to depreciation.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Depreciation_Profile_Reference" type="wd:Depreciation_ProfileObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A reference to the depreciation profile used by this asset.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Depreciation_Method_Reference" type="wd:Abstract_Depreciation_MethodObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A reference to the depreciation method used by this asset, e.g. Straight Line, Sum of Years Digits</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Depreciation_Posting_Frequency_Reference" type="wd:Depreciation_Posting_FrequencyObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A reference to the depreciation posting frequency for this asset.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Depreciation_Convention_Reference" type="wd:Depreciation_Convention__Mixed_ObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A reference to the depreciation convention for this asset, e.g. Current Period, Mid-Month</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Depreciation_Start_Based_On_Reference" type="wd:Abstract_Place_In_Service_Based_OnObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A reference to an indicator for when depreciation starts for this asset, e.g. Upon Acquisition, Manually/When Issued</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Depreciation_Rate_Basis_Reference" type="wd:Depreciation_Rate_BasisObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A reference to the rate bases for depreciation, e.g. Periods, Number of Days</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Depreciation_Start_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The date depreciation started for this asset.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Useful_Life" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The useful life, in periods, for this asset.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="18"/>
<xsd:minInclusive value="0"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Depreciation_Percent" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The depreciation percent for this asset.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Depreciation_Threshold" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The depreciation threshold for this asset.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="30"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="10"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Depreciation_Start_Date_At_Registration" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The deprecation start date as indicated for a converted asset when it was registered.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Accumulated_Depreciation_At_Registration" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The accumulated depreication as indicated for a converted asset when it was registered.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Remaining_Useful_Life_At_Registration" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The remaining useful life as indicated for a converted asset when it was registered.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="18"/>
<xsd:minInclusive value="0"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Max_Bonus_Depreciable_Basis" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The maximum allowable bonus depreciation that can be taken for a particular asset, i.e. the upper limit for depreciation.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Bonus_Depreciation_Percent" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The percentage that will be used to calculate the depreciable basis for bonus depreciation.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="14"/>
<xsd:minInclusive value="0"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="2"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Historical_Bonus_Depreciation_for_Depreciation_Schedule" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The total amount of bonus depreciation recorded for the asset.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Asset_Custodian_WWS_DataType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Contains information about each time this asset was Issued to a Worker or Transferred.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Transaction_Effective_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The transaction effective date of this asset issue or asset transfer activity.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Issued_To_Worker_Reference" type="wd:WorkerObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The Worker the asset was issued or transferred to, if available.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Worktag_Reference" type="wd:Accounting_WorktagObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The worktags specified on this issue or transfer activity, including the new Location for the asset.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Asset_Cost_Adjustment_WWS_DataType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Contains data for cost adjustment activity for this asset.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Transaction_Effective_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The date of the asset cost adjustment.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Cost_Adjustment_Amount" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The amount the asset's cost was adjusted.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="18"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="3"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Cost_Adjustment_Reason_Reference" type="wd:Asset_Cost_Adjustment_ReasonObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A reference to the reason the asset's cost was adjusted.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Residual_Value_Adjustment" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The amount the residual value of the asset was adjusted.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="18"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="3"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Supplier_Invoice_Line_Reference" type="wd:Business_Document_LineObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A reference to a supplier invoice line, if there was one related to the cost adjustment associated with this asset, e.g. due to an improvement or installation cost.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Credit_Card_Transaction_Name_Match_DataType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Element containing Credit Card Transaction Name matches for Travel Cities and Merchants.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Credit Card Transaction Name Match must include either a Merchant, Origination City, or a Destination City as a match.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Confidence level percentage must between 0 and 100.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Credit Card Transaction matches should only include 1 match of either an Origin City, Destination City, or Merchant (Hotel, Airline, or Car Rental Agency).</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Confidence_Percentage" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Confidence level percentage of merchant, or travel city names matching Workday's persisted data.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="6"/>
<xsd:minInclusive value="0"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="3"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Merchant_Reference" type="wd:Abstract_Spend_Data_NameObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Merchant matching the merchant listed on the Credit Card Transaction.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>If a Merchant Reference is provided, it must be a Merchant, or an Alternate Name linked to a Merchant.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Origination_City_Reference" type="wd:Abstract_Spend_Data_NameObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Workday Origination City matching the origination city on the Credit Card Transaction.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>If a Origination City Reference is provided, it must be a Travel City, or an Alternate Name linked to a Travel City.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Destination_City_Reference" type="wd:Abstract_Spend_Data_NameObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Workday Destination City matching the destination city on the Credit Card Transaction.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>If a Destination City Reference is provided, it must be a Travel City, or an Alternate Name linked to a Travel City.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Supplier_Reference" type="wd:Abstract_Payee_Data_NameObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Workday Supplier matching the Supplier on the Credit Card Transaction.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Common_Reference_ID_Type>Supplier_Reference_ID</wd:Common_Reference_ID_Type>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>If a Supplier Reference is provided, it must be a Supplier, or an Alternate Name linked to a Supplier.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Asset_Book_Rule_Request_CriteriaType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Element containing request criteria for the asset book rules operation</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Books_Reference" type="wd:Asset_BookObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to an existing asset book to which the asset book rule data applies</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Asset_Book_Rule_Response_GroupType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Element containing response group for the asset book rules operation</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Travel_City_Alternate_Name_DataType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Element used to specify alternate names.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>There can't be duplicate alternate city names per Country.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Enter a unique Travel City name. [travel_city] is already in use as an alternate name.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Enter a unique Travel City. [alternate_name] is already in use as an alternate name.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Spend_Data_Alternate_Name_Reference" type="wd:Unique_IdentifierObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to the Alternate Name of Travel City.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Alternate_Name" type="xsd:string" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Travel city alternate name.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Impair_Asset_WWS_DataType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Contains data used to process the asset impairment.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Reference" type="wd:Business_AssetObjectType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A reference to the asset that will be impaired.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Common_Reference_ID_Type>Asset_ID</wd:Common_Reference_ID_Type>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The asset specified cannot currently be impaired because it has other activity in progress.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The provided Asset cannot currently have its cost adjusted.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Impairment cannot be performed on Discrete Composite Asset or Components of Non-Discrete Composite Asset.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>The asset is part of a lease contract. You can't impair leased assets.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The asset is part of a lease contract. You can't impair leased assets.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Transaction_Effective_Date" type="xsd:date" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The transaction effective date for the asset impairment. This date cannot be before the acquisition date, in service date, the last cost adjustment or impairment date for the asset. The ledger period status must be valid for this date.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Impairment Date (transaction effective date) cannot be prior to Date Acquired</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Impairment Date (transaction effective date) cannot be prior to last post acquisition adjustment date, last impairment date or last useful life adjustment date.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Impairment Date (transaction effective date) cannot be prior to Date Placed in Service.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Depreciation Start Date for Impairment cannot be prior to Last Resume Date.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Ledger period must exist for the impair depreciation start date.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="New_Market_Value" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Workday calculates the impairment amount as Current Market Value – New Market Value. For a negative cost asset, enter a negative amount for the New Market Value that is greater than the Current Market Value and the Residual Value. For a positive cost asset, enter a positive amount for the New Market Value that is less than the Current Market Value and the Residual Value.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>The new market value entered has too many digits beyond the decimal point</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The new market value entered has too many digits beyond the decimal point</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>New Market Value cannot be negative.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>New Market Value cannot be positive.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Enter a New Market Value that's greater than the Current Market Value.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Enter a New Market Value that's less than the residual value.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Enter a New Market Value that's less than the Current Market Value.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Enter a New Market Value that's greater than the residual value.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Impairment_Reason_Reference" type="wd:Asset_Impairment_ReasonObjectType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A reference to the Asset Impairment Reason for this activity.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Restricted_to_Books_Reference" type="wd:Asset_BookObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to asset books that are used by the asset. Enter asset books if you want to restrict the impairment to specific books. To enact this lifecycle event for all asset books, leave this field blank.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Restricted to Book is required when the asset has at least one fully depreciated book</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>At least one of the Restricted to Books is not valid for asset. Only assets already defined and not loaded into Workday or transferred from different company fully depreciated are valid.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Specify books with the same currency.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Comment" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>An optional comment text to include with the asset impairment.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Impair_Asset_RequestType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Root element for the Request on the Impair Asset operation.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Business_Process_Parameters" type="wd:Financials_Business_Process_ParametersType" minOccurs="0"/>
<xsd:element name="Impair_Asset_Data" type="wd:Impair_Asset_WWS_DataType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Contains data used to process the asset impairment.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
<xsd:attribute ref="wd:version"/>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Impair_Asset_ResponseType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Root element for the Response on the Put operation.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Impairment_Event_Reference" type="wd:Unique_IdentifierObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A reference to the Asset Impairment Event that was created by the request.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
<xsd:attribute ref="wd:version"/>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Reinstate_Asset_WWS_DataType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A wrapper element containing the data about the asset reinstatement.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Asset has a pending event that need be completed before reinstatement.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>This asset cannot be reinstated because it does not exist in all company asset books. This can occur when a company asset book has been added after the asset was disposed.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Reference" type="wd:Business_AssetObjectType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A reference to the asset that should be reinstated.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Common_Reference_ID_Type>Asset_ID</wd:Common_Reference_ID_Type>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The asset cannot be reinstated because it was transferred to a different company.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The asset cannot be reinstated because it is not disposed.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>There must be a complete supplier contract amendment for the asset before Workday can process this asset transaction.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Comment" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>An optional comment to track with the asset reinstatement event.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Reinstate_Asset_RequestType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Root element for the Request on the Reinstate Asset operation.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Business_Process_Parameters" type="wd:Financials_Business_Process_ParametersType" minOccurs="0"/>
<xsd:element name="Reinstate_Asset_Data" type="wd:Reinstate_Asset_WWS_DataType"/>
</xsd:sequence>
<xsd:attribute ref="wd:version"/>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Reinstate_Asset_ResponseType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Root element for the Response on the Put operation.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Reinstatement_Event_Reference" type="wd:Unique_IdentifierObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A reference to the Reinstatement Event that was created by the request.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
<xsd:attribute ref="wd:version"/>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Dispose_Asset_DataType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Contains data used to process the asset disposal.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The following worktag type(s) are required: [missing]</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The following Dispose Asset Worktag types are invalid: [invalid]</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Reference" type="wd:Business_AssetObjectType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A reference to the asset that should be disposed.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Common_Reference_ID_Type>Asset_ID</wd:Common_Reference_ID_Type>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The asset specified cannot currently be disposed because it has other activity in progress.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>You can only dispose an asset that is In Service, Issued, Registered, or Out of Service. If you register an asset from a lease type supplier contract, the contract must be cancelled or the asset fully depreciated. You can't dispose an asset that is a Discrete Composite Asset.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can only dispose an asset that is In Service, Issued, Registered, or Out of Service. If you register an asset from a lease type supplier contract, the contract must be cancelled or the asset fully depreciated. You can't dispose an asset that is a Discrete Composite Asset.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>There must be a complete supplier contract amendment for the asset before Workday can process this asset transaction.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Transaction_Effective_Date" type="xsd:date" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The transaction effective date for the asset disposal.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The transaction effective date of the disposal is too soon; asset may be expired after the Period End Date of the last depreciation expense line for the life of the asset.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The transaction effective date of the disposal cannot be earlier than the acquisition date.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The transaction effective date of the disposal must be less than or equal to today's date.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The fiscal Period for the transaction date must exist in the fiscal schedule of every company asset book where this is a depreciable asset in order to do this transaction</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Transaction effective date of this transaction cannot be prior to last reclassification date for asset</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Asset has an event with transaction date after this Partial Disposal transaction effective date</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Depreciation effective date for partial disposal cannot be prior to last resume date for the asset.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Transaction Effective Date must be on or after the last Depreciation Date of the asset book.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Disposal_Type_Reference" type="wd:Asset_Disposal_TypeObjectType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A reference to the type of disposal.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Percent_to_Dispose" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The percent of asset total cost to dispose. Valid values between 1 and 100. If percent to dispose is 0 and cost to dispose is 0, percent to dispose will be set 100.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You cannot partially dispose an asset with status of Out of Service</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You cannot partially dispose an expense asset</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You cannot partially dispose expired asset.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Disposal percent must be greater than 0 and less than or equal to 100.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Percent to Dispose must be equal to 100 for leased assets.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="19"/>
<xsd:minInclusive value="0"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="16"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Cost_to_Dispose" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The cost from total asset cost to dispose.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Disposal cost must not be greater than current cost.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>The cost to dispose entered has too many digits beyond the decimal point</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The cost to dispose entered has too many digits beyond the decimal point</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Asset Disposal can't be negative.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Asset Disposal can't be positive.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Disposal cost must not be less than current cost.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The asset disposal cost for leased asset from a supplier contract must be equal to the cost of the asset.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Disposal_Fair_Market_Value" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The fair market value of the asset at the time of disposal.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>The disposal fair market value entered has too many digits beyond the decimal point</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The disposal fair market value entered has too many digits beyond the decimal point</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Sale_Price" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The sale price (if the Disposal Type was Sale) when the asset was sold.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Sale Price can only be entered if the disposal type is a sale.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>The sale price entered has too many digits beyond the decimal point</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The sale price entered has too many digits beyond the decimal point</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Comments" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Free-form comments to include with the disposal event.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Worktag_Reference" type="wd:Accounting_WorktagObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A list of worktags to track with the disposal event.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>One or more of the worktags selected are of an invalid type for this transaction.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Only one worktag for each type is allowed for each disposal activity.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Select a balancing worktag for Worktags of the following type: [type]</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>[non-allowed worktags for asset web service]</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>[missing worktags for business asset web service]</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>'[worktag value]' is not permitted as an allowed value for worktag type: [worktag type] because it is inactive.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>[partitionable] is not allowed to be used by [company].</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Asset is shared by worktags. You cannot update these worktags during disposal.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>[invalid worktag value message]</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Dispose_Asset_RequestType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Root element for the Request on the Dispose Asset operation.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Business_Process_Parameters" type="wd:Financials_Business_Process_ParametersType" minOccurs="0"/>
<xsd:element name="Dispose_Asset_Data" type="wd:Dispose_Asset_DataType"/>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Dispose_Asset_ResponseType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Root element for the Response on the Dispose Asset operation.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Disposal_Event_Reference" type="wd:Unique_IdentifierObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A reference to the Asset Disposal Event that was created by the request.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
<xsd:attribute ref="wd:version"/>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Asset_Depreciation_Detail_DataType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Contains data for deprecation detail transactions for this asset.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Depreciation_Detail_Line_Data" type="wd:Asset_Depreciation_Detail_Line_DataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Asset_Depreciation_Detail_Line_DataType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Contains details for each depreciation expense line for the asset.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Depreciation_Period" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The sequence number of the depreciation line.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="12"/>
<xsd:minInclusive value="0"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="0"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Period_Ending_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The end date of the ledger period this depreciation line is for.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Depreciation_Number_Of_Days" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The number of depreciation days for this transaction.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="12"/>
<xsd:minInclusive value="0"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="0"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Period_Depreciation_Amount" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The amount of depreciation recorded for this transaction.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="18"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="3"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Worktag_Reference" type="wd:Audited_Accounting_WorktagObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>References to worktags associated with this depreciation expense.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Depreciation_Adjustment_Transaction_Type" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The type of transaction for this depreciation transaction.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Bonus_Depreciation" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Any bonus depreciation applied for this transaction.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Recorded_On_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The date this depreciation activity was recorded on. If it has not been recorded yet, this value is blank.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Contingent_Worker_Receipt_Line_Replacement_DataType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Contingent Worker Receipt Line Replacement Data. For logging time worked.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Purchase Order Line Reference must be for a Contingent Worker Order Line.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Purchase Order Line must be from an issued Order.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Purchase Order Line must be for the same Company as the Receipt.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Purchase Order Line must be for the same Supplier as the Receipt.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Period Start Date is not within the date range for the purchase order line referenced. Check the date range for the purchase order line and select a new date.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Period End Date is not within the date range for the purchase order line referenced. Check the date range for the purchase order line and select a new date.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Period End Date should be greater than or equal to Start Date.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You are updating an existing Receipt (referenced by the Receipt Number or Receipt Reference). The existing Receipt has a Purchase Order ([po1]) that does not match the Purchase Order for this Contingent Worker Receipt ([po2]).</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The "Amount to Receive" ([receive amt]) does not match the expected amount calculated ([calculated amt]) from the Hours Worked and Additional Amount entered.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>The Purchase Order Line referenced is from a PO that is Closed or Pending Close.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Purchase Order Line referenced is from a PO that is Closed or Pending Close.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Purchase Order Line cannot be used because it has been Canceled.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Purchase Order Line Number [PO Line] cannot be used because it has been canceled.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Purchase_Order_Line_Reference" type="wd:Purchase_Order_LineObjectType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Purchase Order Line associated with the Contingent Worker Receipt Line</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Invalid ID value.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Period_Start_Date" type="xsd:date" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Start Date for the Period defined.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Period_End_Date" type="xsd:date" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>End Date for the Period defined.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Hours_Worked_Data" type="wd:Hours_Worked_DataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Hours Worked details.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Additional_Amount" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Additional amount, if any, for the Receipt Line which is not associated with Hours Worked.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:minInclusive value="0"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Amount_to_Receive" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Calculated Amount to Receive based on sum of Hours Worked Data plus Additional Amount (if any). The Hours Worked Amount is calculated based on the Time Code Rate Multiplier and the Contract Pay Rate on the Purchase Order Line.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="18"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="3"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Memo" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Memo for the Receipt Line.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Hours_Worked_DataType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Hours Worked Data. Contains the applicable time code and number of hours worked.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Negative hours are not allowed. Please enter a positive number of hours.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Time_Code_Reference" type="wd:Time_Entry_CodeObjectType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Time Code for the hours worked. For example, Regular or Overtime.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Time Code entered ([time code]) is not valid for the Purchase Order Line ([line]).</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Hours" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Hours worked.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="14"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="2"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Asset_Book_Configurations_Request_ReferencesType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The Request References element contains the specific instance set that should be returned in the Get operation. Only the Workday ID (GUID) should be specified for each instance to be returned.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Book_Configuration_Reference" type="wd:Unique_IdentifierObjectType" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>References to existing Asset Book Configuration to return data for in the response.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Asset_Book_Configurations_Request_CriteriaType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The Request Criteria is a wrapper element around a list of elements representing the operation specific criteria needed to search for asset depreciation schedules</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Company_Reference" type="wd:CompanyObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>One or more Company references to use to filter the asset depreciation schedules returned in the response.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Name" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>An Asset Name value to be used to return asset depreciation schedules for an existing asset with the matching Asset Name value.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Book_Reference" type="wd:Asset_BookObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>One or more Asset Books to return asset depreciation schedule for these books</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>One or more of the asset books in the request is Accounting Book. This web service does not support accounting books.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Spend_Category_Reference" type="wd:Spend_CategoryObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>One or more Spend Category(s) of assets to return asset depreciation schedules for assets in those categories.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>At least one spend category is not a trackable. Business assets support only trackable categories.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Class_Reference" type="wd:Asset_ClassObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>One or more Asset Class(s) to return asset depreciation schedules for assets in those classes</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Type_Reference" type="wd:Asset_TypeObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>One or more Asset Type(s) to return asset depreciation schedules for assets in those types</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Location_Reference" type="wd:LocationObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>One or more Locations to returns asset depreciation schedules for assets currently placed in those locations.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Worktags_Reference" type="wd:Accounting_WorktagObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>One or more Worktag references to be used to return asset depreciation schedules for Assets currently assigned any of these worktags. To filter based on Location, use the Location Reference element.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Acquired_From_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Allows you to return asset depreciation schedule for assets by the date they were acquired. This is the From Date to find assets by acquisition date. This date is inclusive.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Acquired_To_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Allows you to return asset depreciation schedules for assets by the date they were acquired. This is the To Date to find assets by acquisition date. This date is inclusive.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="In_Service_From_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Allows you to return asset depreciation schedules by the date they were placed in service. This is the From Date to find asset depreciation schedules by in service date. This date is inclusive.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="In_Service_To_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Allows you to return asset depreciation schedules by the date they were placed in service. This is the To Date to find asset depreciation schedules by in service date. This date is inclusive.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Depreciation_Schedule_Status_Reference" type="wd:Document_StatusObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Enter an Asset Depreciation Schedule Status reference to return schedules currently in that status. Valid values for depreciation schedule status is In Service, Registered and disposed. Don't enter a status reference to return schedules in any status.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>At least one of the asset depreciation schedule statuses is not valid. Valid values are: Registered, In Service, Disposed, or Removed.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Acquisition_Method_Reference" type="wd:Acquisition_MethodObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>One or more Acquisition Method references to return asset depreciation schedules for assets acquired using one of those methods.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Accounting_Treatment_Reference" type="wd:Accounting_TreatmentObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>One or more Accounting Treatment references to return asset depreciation schedules with those accounting treatments. A depreciation schedule can have accounting treatment of Expense, Depreciable, or Non-Depreciable.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Exclude_Schedules_with_Historical_Information" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Allows you to return asset depreciation schedules with no historical information such as accumulated depreciation. Enter 1 to exclude asset depreciation schedules with historical information.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Get_Asset_Book_Configurations_RequestType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Root element for the Request on the Get operation. Contains references, criteria and filter for specifying which instances to return in the Response.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:choice>
<xsd:element name="Request_References" type="wd:Asset_Book_Configurations_Request_ReferencesType" minOccurs="0"/>
<xsd:element name="Request_Criteria" type="wd:Asset_Book_Configurations_Request_CriteriaType" minOccurs="0"/>
</xsd:choice>
<xsd:element name="Response_Filter" type="wd:Response_FilterType" minOccurs="0"/>
</xsd:sequence>
<xsd:attribute ref="wd:version"/>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Asset_Depreciation_ScheduleType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Element that contains the Asset Depreciation Schedule reference and data.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Book_Configuration_Reference" type="wd:Unique_IdentifierObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A reference to the asset book configuration</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Book_Configuration_Data" type="wd:Asset_Depreciation_Schedule_DataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Asset_Book_Configuration_Response_DataType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Contains all the Asset Depreciation Schedules returned by the web service operation.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Book_Configuration" type="wd:Asset_Depreciation_ScheduleType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Get_Asset_Book_Configurations_ResponseType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>This element is the top-level response element for all Get Asset Depreciation Schedules operation</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Request_References" type="wd:Asset_Book_Configurations_Request_ReferencesType" minOccurs="0"/>
<xsd:element name="Request_Criteria" type="wd:Asset_Book_Configurations_Request_CriteriaType" minOccurs="0"/>
<xsd:element name="Response_Filter" type="wd:Response_FilterType" minOccurs="0"/>
<xsd:element name="Response_Results" type="wd:Response_ResultsType" minOccurs="0"/>
<xsd:element name="Response_Data" type="wd:Asset_Book_Configuration_Response_DataType" minOccurs="0"/>
</xsd:sequence>
<xsd:attribute ref="wd:version"/>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Asset_Depreciation_Schedule_DataType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Element containing Asset Depreciation Schedule data that may be updated by Update Asset Depreciation Schedule operation.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Specify an Original Acquisition Cost or Residual Value only for assets that don't have accounting for the acquisition in this asset book: [asset book].</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Specify a valid value for Residual Value. When Original Acquisition Cost is negative, the residual value must be greater than or equal to the acquisition cost.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Specify a valid value for Residual Value. When Original Acquisition Cost is positive, the residual value must be lower than or equal to the acquisition cost.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You must specify a value for Original Acquisition Cost when adding an asset book to an asset.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Specify an Original Acquisition Cost or Residual Value only for assets that don't have lifecycle events in this asset book: [asset book].</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Specify cost information only for assets that don't have any accounting or lifecycle events in this asset book: [asset book]. This asset is attached to a supplier invoice. Specify a different asset or cancel the supplier invoice and try again.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The asset is restricted to specific asset books based on spend category, supplier contract type, or lease accounting method. Specify asset books that meet the company asset book restrictions.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>When you select the Depreciation Method as Rate Schedule, ensure that you select the Depreciation Convention as 1 of these: [allowed depreciation conventions].[Restrict NoD]</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Add_Only" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Add Only Flag. Indicates that the service is an add only, not an update.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Asset_ID" type="xsd:string" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The primary ID of the asset of this asset depreciation schedule. The value of this field and the asset book reference represent a unique ID that can be used to identify this asset depreciation schedule instance</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Asset ID does not exist in the system</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>There is a pending event for the asset that should be completed before this asset transaction can be processed.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>There is a pending event for the asset that should be completed before this asset transaction can be processed.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>There must be a complete supplier contract amendment for the asset before Workday can process this asset transaction.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Specify an asset book for the component of a discrete asset. You can't specify the asset book for parent of a discrete asset.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Specify an asset book for the parent of a non-discrete asset. You can't specify the asset book for components of a non-discrete asset.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Specify an asset with a valid status. You can't specify an asset with a Removed status.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Specify an asset with a valid status. You can't specify an asset with a Disposed status.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Currency Conversion Rates between currency and company's alternate ledger currency are not defined.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Specify a valid ID. The ID you submitted is invalid for your request.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Book_Reference" type="wd:Asset_BookObjectType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>This is the reference id value to an asset book used by the asset company. A value is required for every asset depreciation schedule. The value of this book cannot be the primary book for the asset company.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can’t update a depreciation schedule if the schedule contains depreciation lines with Accounted Status. To update depreciation schedules with Accounted Status lines, use the Override Depreciation Period Status task to override the status.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't update asset books with posted depreciation.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You must specify an existing asset book for an asset before you update the asset book.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You must first set up the company asset book to be able to specify the Asset Book ID for this asset: [asset].</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>This asset book already exists for the asset [asset]: [book]. Specify a different asset book, or remove the add only flag.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Specify a Depreciation Start Date that’s after the Alternate Ledger Currency Fiscal Start Year for the Asset Book and Company that you specify.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Accounting_Treatment_Reference" type="wd:Accounting_TreatmentObjectType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>This is the reference id value to an existing accounting treatment. Workday supplies the accounting treatments Expense, Depreciable Capital and Non-Depreciable Capital. It is required for every asset depreciation schedule.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Select a valid accounting treatment. The Inventory Asset accounting treatment isn’t valid for assets.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Depreciation_Profile_Reference" type="wd:Depreciation_ProfileObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to depreciation profile used by this asset depreciation schedule. It is required of the accounting treatment is depreciable capital.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Depreciation Profile is required when accounting treatment is Depreciable Capital</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Depreciation Profile is required when accounting treatment is Depreciable Capital</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Depreciation profile must be blank when accounting treatment is not depreciable capital</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Depreciation profile must be blank when accounting treatment is not depreciable capital</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Contract start date and contract end date are required for selected depreciation method.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Specify an active depreciation profile. This depreciation profile is inactive: [depreciation profile].</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Depreciation_Convention_Reference" type="wd:Depreciation_Convention__Mixed_ObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to depreciation convention used by this asset depreciation schedule. It is required if the accounting treatment is depreciable capital.In order to assign 'Half-Year' as the depreciation convention, the company asset book must use a fiscal schedule with an even number of fiscal periods per fiscal year.In order to assign 'Mid-Quarter' as the depreciation convention, the company asset book must use a fiscal schedule where number of fiscal periods per fiscal year is divisible by 4.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Depreciation convention must be blank when accounting treatment is not depreciable capital</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Depreciation convention must be blank when accounting treatment is not depreciable capital</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Depreciation Convention is required when accounting treatment is depreciable capital</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Depreciation Convention is required when accounting treatment is depreciable capital</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Depreciation_Method_Reference" type="wd:Abstract_Depreciation_MethodObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to depreciation method used by this asset depreciation schedule. It is required if the accounting treatment is depreciable capital</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Depreciation Method is required when accounting treatment is Depreciable Capital</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Depreciation Method is required when accounting treatment is Depreciable Capital</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Depreciation method must be blank when accounting treatment is not depreciable capital</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Depreciation method must be blank when accounting treatment is not depreciable capital</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The selected Depreciation Convention can't be used with a depreciation method of [Depreciation Method].</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Depreciation_Percent" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Numeric value representing the depreciation percent for Declining Balance with Switch to Straight Line method. It is required when the depreciation method is declining balance. It left blank, it will be defaulted from the depreciation profile.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Depreciation percent must be zero unless you are using Declining Balance or Declining Balance Switch to Straight Line Depreciation Methods.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Depreciation percent must be zero unless you are using Declining Balance or Declining Balance Switch to Straight Line Depreciation Methods.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Depreciation percent should be greater than 100 when the depreciation method is Declining Balance Switch to SL.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Depreciation percent should be greater than 100 when the depreciation method is Declining Balance Switch to SL.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Depreciation percent must be greater than 0 and less than 100 when the depreciation method is Declining Balance.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Depreciation percent must be greater than 0 and less than 100 when the depreciation method is Declining Balance.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Enter Depreciation Percent when overriding depreciation profile information and depreciation method is Declining Balance (with and without switch to Straight Line).</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Enter Depreciation Percent when overriding depreciation profile information and depreciation method is Declining Balance (with and without switch to Straight Line).</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="18"/>
<xsd:minInclusive value="0"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Useful_Life__Periods_" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Numeric value representing the useful life (in periods) for the asset depreciation schedule. It is required if the accounting treatment is depreciable capital. If left blank it will be defaulted from the depreciation profile.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Useful Life cannot be more than 200 years. Useful life in years is useful life in periods divided by number of periods in the company's fiscal year.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Useful Life cannot be more than 200 years. Useful life in years is useful life in periods divided by number of periods in the company's fiscal year.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Useful life in periods must be 0 when accounting treatment is expense</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Useful Life must be equal to zero if the Depreciation Method is Declining Balance.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Useful Life must be equal to zero if the Depreciation Method is Declining Balance.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't enter the Useful Life for an asset with a depreciation method of Term because the Useful Life is derived from the contract start and end dates.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't enter the Useful Life for an asset with a depreciation method of Rate Schedule because the Useful Life is derived from the length of the rate schedule.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Useful life in periods is required when accounting treatment is depreciable capital (and depreciation method is not Declining Balance, Term or Rate Schedule).</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="12"/>
<xsd:minInclusive value="0"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="0"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Depreciation_Threshold" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Depreciation Threshold. Enter only if method is declining balance.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Only Declining Balance Depreciation Method can have a threshold.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Only Declining Balance Depreciation Method can have a threshold.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Declining Balance Depreciation Method must have a threshold.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Declining Balance Depreciation Method must have a threshold.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Depreciation Threshold is greater than Total Asset Cost.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Depreciation Threshold is greater than Total Asset Cost.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Depreciation Threshold is less than Total Asset Cost.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Depreciation Threshold cannot be positive.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Depreciation Threshold cannot be negative.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The depreciation threshold entered has too many digits beyond the decimal point.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="21"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Contract_Start_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Workday uses these dates to update External Contract Start and End date if you manually register the asset but updates the In service Start and End date for all other sources.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Contract start date must have same value as Date Acquired</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You cannot update the contract start or contract end date for assets that are from a supplier contract.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Contract_End_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Workday uses these dates to update External Contract Start and End date if you manually register the asset but updates the In service Start and End date for all other sources.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Contract End Date cannot be before the date an asset is acquired.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Contract End Date cannot be before the Contract Start Date.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Date_Placed_in_Service" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Date value representing the date this asset depreciation schedule is placed in service. It is required if the depreciation schedule has historical information. It cannot be after depreciation start date and prior to the asset acquisition date.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Date placed in service must be blank when accounting treatment is not depreciable capital</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Date placed in service must be blank when accounting treatment is not depreciable capital</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Date placed in service must be the same as asset acquisition date or must be left blank when Place in Service option is Upon Acquisition</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Date placed in service must be the same as asset acquisition date or must be left blank when Place in Service option is Upon Acquisition</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Date placed in service cannot be after the date the asset first issued.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Date placed in service cannot be after the date the asset first issued.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Date placed in service cannot be after depreciation start date</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Date placed in service cannot be after depreciation start date</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Date placed in service cannot be prior to date acquired</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Date placed in service cannot be prior to date acquired</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Bonus_Depreciation_Percent" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Numeric value representing bonus depreciation percent for this asset depreciation schedule. Value cannot be more than 100.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Bonus depreciation percent is required when historical bonus depreciation amount is not 0</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Bonus depreciation percent must be 0 when accounting treatment is not depreciable capital</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Bonus depreciation percent must be 0 when accounting treatment is not depreciable capital</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Bonus depreciation percent cannot be more than 100</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Bonus depreciation percent cannot be more than 100</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="14"/>
<xsd:minInclusive value="0"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="2"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Max_Bonus_Depreciable_Basis" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Numeric value representing the maximum bonus depreciation basis. Workday would use the lesser of this field and asset cost that is applicable to bonus depreciation to calculated the bonus amount.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Max Depreciable Basis must be 0 when accounting treatment is not depreciable capital</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Max Depreciable Basis must be 0 when accounting treatment is not depreciable capital</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>The max bonus depreciable basis entered has too many digits beyond the decimal point</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The max bonus depreciable basis entered has too many digits beyond the decimal point</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Depreciation_Start_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>For converted assets, the depreciation start date represents the date that depreciation starts in Workday. For converted assets with historical accumulated depreciation, the depreciation start date should be 1 day greater than the date up to which the historical accumulated depreciation is calculated. The date cannot be prior to the acquisition date. For converted assets with no historical accumulated depreciation, leave the depreciation start date blank so that Workday can determine the correct date.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Depreciation Start Date cannot be prior to acquisition date of the asset</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Depreciation Start Date cannot be prior to acquisition date of the asset</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Fiscal period must exist in fiscal schedule for depreciation start date</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Fiscal period must exist in fiscal schedule for depreciation start date</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Depreciation Start Date must match start date of the first fiscal period that depreciation is to start in Workday.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Depreciation Start Date must match start date of the first fiscal period that depreciation is to start in Workday.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Depreciation start date must be blank when accounting treatment is not depreciable capital</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Depreciation start date must be blank when accounting treatment is not depreciable capital</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>You cannot update depreciation schedule historical information if the schedule was created by Intercompany Transfer transaction</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You cannot update depreciation schedule historical information if the schedule was created by Intercompany Transfer transaction</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Depreciation start date cannot be prior to the effective transaction date of an adjustment if the remaining depreciation periods is 0</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Depreciation start date cannot be prior to the effective transaction date of an adjustment if the remaining depreciation periods is 0</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Depreciation Start Date cannot be prior to the date the asset was transferred to this company</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Depreciation Start Date cannot be prior to the date the asset was transferred to this company</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Remaining_Depreciation_Periods" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Numeric value for remaining depreciation periods if entering accumulated depreciation from a prior system and depreciation start date. Workday will generate depreciation entries for this schedule for the number of remaining periods.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Remaining depreciation periods is required when you enter Accumulated Depreciation</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Remaining depreciation periods is required when you enter Accumulated Depreciation</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>The fiscal period must exist for the depreciation start date in the fiscal schedule for the company asset book.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The fiscal period must exist for the depreciation start date in the fiscal schedule for the company asset book.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Remaining depreciation periods must be 0 when depreciation start date is blank</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Remaining depreciation periods must be 0 when depreciation start date is blank</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Remaining depreciation periods cannot be greater than useful life</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Remaining depreciation periods cannot be greater than useful life</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>When depreciation is based on the number of days per period, all the fiscal years / periods for an asset's useful life must already be created in order to calculate the depreciation amount for each period correctly. In order to complete the depreciation setup for this asset and create the depreciation schedule, you will need to create additional fiscal years / periods for fiscal schedule linked to the company asset book(s).</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>When depreciation is based on the number of days per period, all the fiscal years / periods for an asset's useful life must already be created in order to calculate the depreciation amount for each period correctly. In order to complete the depreciation setup for this asset and create the depreciation schedule, you will need to create additional fiscal years / periods for fiscal schedule linked to the company asset book(s).</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>When depreciation is based on the number of days per period, all the fiscal years / periods for an asset's useful life must already be created in order to calculate the depreciation amount for each period correctly. In order to complete the depreciation setup for this asset and create the depreciation schedule, you will need to create additional fiscal years / periods for fiscal schedule linked to the company asset book(s).</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>When depreciation is based on the number of days per period, all the fiscal years / periods for an asset's useful life must already be created in order to calculate the depreciation amount for each period correctly. In order to complete the depreciation setup for this asset and create the depreciation schedule, you will need to create additional fiscal years / periods for fiscal schedule linked to the company asset book(s).</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="18"/>
<xsd:minInclusive value="0"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Original_Acquisition_Cost" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The Unit Cost of Asset for the specified Book</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The acquisition cost entered has too many digits beyond the decimal point</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Total_Asset_Cost" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>This field is for display only, any values updated will be ignored.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Residual_Value" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Residual or salvage value for the specified Book</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The residual value entered has too many digits beyond the decimal point</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Fair_Market_Value" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Fair Market Value for the specified book</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The fair market value entered has too many digits beyond the decimal point</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Accumulated_Depreciation" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Numeric value representing historical accumulated depreciation as of a day prior to depreciation start date. This value cannot be greater than historical cost minus historical residual value. Workday uses this accumulated depreciation value to determine depreciable cost basis to generate the depreciation schedule for remaining useful life starting from depreciation start date.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Accumulated depreciation cannot be greater than cost minus residual value for the asset book</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Accumulated depreciation cannot be greater than cost minus residual value for the asset book</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Accumulated depreciation must be 0 when depreciation start date is blank</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Accumulated depreciation must be 0 when depreciation start date is blank</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Accumulated depreciation is required when depreciation start date has a value</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Accumulated depreciation is required when depreciation start date has a value</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>The accumulated depreciation entered has too many digits beyond the decimal point</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The accumulated depreciation entered has too many digits beyond the decimal point</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Accumulated depreciation cannot be less than cost minus residual value for the asset book.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Year_to_Date_Depreciation" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Numeric value representing year-to-date depreciation as of a day period to depreciation start date. This field is required if the asset depreciation schedule has historical information and the depreciation method is either declining balance or sum of years digits. The value of this field cannot be greater than historical accumulated depreciation.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Year To Date depreciation cannot be greater than accumulated depreciation</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Year To Date depreciation cannot be greater than accumulated depreciation</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>The year to date depreciation entered has too many digits beyond the decimal point</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The year to date depreciation entered has too many digits beyond the decimal point</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Year To Date depreciation cannot be less than accumulated depreciation.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Year to date depreciation is required if depreciation method is Declining Balance with Switch to Straight Line or Sum of Years and depreciation start date is not in the first period of the fiscal year</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Year to date depreciation is required if depreciation method is Declining Balance with Switch to Straight Line or Sum of Years and depreciation start date is not in the first period of the fiscal year</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Historical_Bonus_Depreciation" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Numeric value representing historical bonus depreciation amount. This field is required if the depreciation schedule has historical information and bonus depreciation percent is populated, else it should be left empty. The value of this field cannot be greater than accumulated depreciation.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Historical bonus depreciation amount must be 0 when accounting treatment is not depreciable capital</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Historical bonus depreciation amount must be 0 when accounting treatment is not depreciable capital</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Historical bonus depreciation amount cannot be greater than accumulated depreciation</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Historical bonus depreciation amount cannot be greater than accumulated depreciation</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Historical bonus depreciation amount is required when bonus depreciation percent has a value and asset depreciation schedule has historical inforamtion</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>The historical bonus depreciation entered has too many digits beyond the decimal point</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The historical bonus depreciation entered has too many digits beyond the decimal point</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Historical bonus depreciation amount cannot be less than accumulated depreciation.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Book_Configuration_Additional_Data" type="wd:Asset_Depreciation_Schedule_Additional_InformationType" minOccurs="0"/>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Data" type="wd:Asset_for_Depreciation_Schedule_DataType" minOccurs="0"/>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Asset_for_Depreciation_Schedule_DataType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Contains information about the asset to which asset depreciation schedule belongs</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Company_Reference" type="wd:CompanyObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A reference to the Company this asset belongs to.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Common_Reference_ID_Type>Company_Reference_ID</wd:Common_Reference_ID_Type>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Name" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The name of the asset.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Spend_Category_Reference" type="wd:Spend_CategoryObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A reference to the Spend Category this asset belongs to.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Class_Reference" type="wd:Asset_ClassObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A reference to the Asset Class for this asset.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Type_Reference" type="wd:Asset_TypeObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A reference to the Asset Type for this asset.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Location_Reference" type="wd:LocationObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A reference to the current location of the asset</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Acquisition_Method_Reference" type="wd:Acquisition_MethodObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A reference to the Acquisition Method this asset was acquired with.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Date_Acquired" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The date the asset was acquired, or the transaction effective date of the acquisition.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="First_Issue_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The date the asset was first issued to a worker</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Update_Asset_Book_Configuration_RequestType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Element that contains an Asset Reference and Asset Book Reference and corresponding data for asset depreciation schedule to be updated</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Book_Configuration_Data" type="wd:Asset_Depreciation_Schedule_DataType" minOccurs="0"/>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Update_Asset_Book_Configuration_ResponseType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Root element for the Response on the Put operation.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Update_Asset_Depreciation_Schedule_Reference" type="wd:Unique_IdentifierObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to an existing Asset Depreciation Schedule</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
<xsd:attribute ref="wd:version"/>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Asset_Depreciation_Schedule_Additional_InformationType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Element containing Asset Depreciation Schedule additional information that will not be updated by updated by Update Asset Depreciation</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Book_Configuration_Status_Reference" type="wd:Document_StatusObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A reference to the status of the asset book configuration</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Historical_Cost_Balance" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A numeric value that represents historical cost balance for depreciation schedule. Historical cost are those transactions with transaction effective date prior to depreciation start date.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>The historical cost balance entered has too many digits beyond the decimal point</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The historical cost balance entered has too many digits beyond the decimal point</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Remove_Asset_DataType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Contains data used to process the asset removal.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Reference" type="wd:Business_AssetObjectType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A reference to the asset that should be removed.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The asset specified cannot currently be removed because it has other activity in progress.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>An asset can only be removed if its events are limited to issue and transfer, and it was either manually registered or registered from a Receipt or Supplier Invoice that is now canceled. If registered from a lease type Supplier Contract the contract must be canceled. Assets that are Discrete Composite Asset or Components of Non-Discrete Composite Asset cannot be removed.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>An asset can only be removed if its events are limited to issue and transfer, and it was either manually registered or registered from a Receipt or Supplier Invoice that is now canceled. If registered from a lease type Supplier Contract the contract must be canceled. Assets that are Discrete Composite Asset or Components of Non-Discrete Composite Asset cannot be removed.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>There must be a complete supplier contract amendment for the asset before Workday can process this asset transaction.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Asset cannot be removed when referencing invalid supplier invoice lines.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The supplier invoice line has changed and is no longer valid:[validations]</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Transaction_Effective_Date" type="xsd:date" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The transaction effective date for the asset removal.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Asset has an event with transaction date after Remove transaction effective date</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The transaction effective date must be less than or equal to today's date.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The transaction effective date is prior to this asset's conversion into Workday. The portion of accumulated depreciation that represents depreciation taken in a prior system will not be included in the depreciation recalculation in Workday.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Removal_Reason_Reference" type="wd:Asset_Removal_ReasonObjectType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A reference to the removal reason for the asset.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Removal_Comments" type="xsd:string" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Free-form comments to include with the removal event.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Remove_Asset_RequestType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Root element for the Request on the Remove Asset operation.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Business_Process_Parameters" type="wd:Financials_Business_Process_ParametersType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Contains data for business processing</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Remove_Asset_Data" type="wd:Remove_Asset_DataType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Contains data used to process the asset removal.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
<xsd:attribute ref="wd:version"/>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Remove_Asset_ResponseType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Root element for the Response on the Remove Asset operation.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Removal_Event__CL__Reference" type="wd:Unique_IdentifierObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A reference to the Asset Removal Event that was created by the request.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
<xsd:attribute ref="wd:version"/>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Cancel_Receipt_RequestType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Cancel Receipt Request</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>You cannot cancel a Receipt that will result in the Quantity Returned to be greater than the Approved Receipts Quantity. Please cancel the Return before canceling the Receipt, or change the Quantity Returned to be less than the Approved Receipts Quantity.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You cannot cancel a Receipt that will result in the Quantity Returned to be greater than the Approved Receipts Quantity. Please cancel the Return before canceling the Receipt, or change the Quantity Returned to be less than the Approved Receipts Quantity.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't cancel the receipt as 1 or more associated PO lines are closed for receiving.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Cancel_Receipt_Reference" type="wd:ReceiptObjectType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to an existing Receipt</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>This Receipt is not Cancelable.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
<xsd:attribute ref="wd:version"/>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Cancel_Receipt_ResponseType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Cancel Receipt Response</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Cancel_Receipt_Reference" type="wd:ReceiptObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to an existing Receipt</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
<xsd:attribute ref="wd:version"/>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Asset_Reclassification_WWS_DataType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Contains data for each time an asset was reclassified. An asset may have more than one reclassification activity.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Transaction_Effective_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The date the asset was reclassified</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Item_Descriptor_Reference" type="wd:Item_DescriptorObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A reference to the item descriptor</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Spend_Category_Reference" type="wd:Spend_CategoryObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A reference to the spend category of the reclassification activity</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Type_Reference" type="wd:Asset_TypeObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A reference to the asset type of the reclassification activity</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Class_Reference" type="wd:Asset_ClassObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A reference to the asset class of the reclassification activity</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Useful_Life" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The new useful life for reclassification activity. Value is 0 if useful life did not change</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="12"/>
<xsd:minInclusive value="0"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="0"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Asset_Removal_WWS_DataType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Contains data for removal activity for this asset.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Transaction_Effective_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The date of the asset removal</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Removal_Reason_Reference" type="wd:Asset_Removal_ReasonObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A reference to the reason the asset was removed</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Comments" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Comments entered by the user when removing the asset.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Address_ReferenceType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The address Reference ID.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The field ID is required and must have a value.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="ID" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Unique Reference ID for Address</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Put_Import_Process_ResponseType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Put Import Process Response element</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Import_Process_Reference" type="wd:Web_Service_Background_Process_RuntimeObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Web Service Background Process Runtime element</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Header_Instance_Reference" type="wd:InstanceObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Header Instance element</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
<xsd:attribute ref="wd:version"/>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Prepaid_Spend_Amortization_Request_CriteriaType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Element containing Prepaid Spend Amortization request criteria</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Supplier_Invoice_Reference" type="wd:Supplier_InvoiceObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to an existing Supplier Invoice for the Prepaid Spend Amortization</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Prepaid_Spend_Amortization_Response_GroupType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Element containing Prepaid Spend Amortization response grouping options</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Include_Reference" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Include Reference</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Get_Prepaid_Spend_Amortizations_RequestType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Contains request reference, criteria, filter and response group for getting Prepaid Spend Amortization data</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Request_Criteria" type="wd:Prepaid_Spend_Amortization_Request_CriteriaType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Get Prepaid Spend Amortization Request Critiera</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Response_Filter" type="wd:Response_FilterType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Get Prepaid Spend Amortization Response Filter</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Response_Group" type="wd:Prepaid_Spend_Amortization_Response_GroupType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Get Prepaid Spend Amortization Response Group</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
<xsd:attribute ref="wd:version"/>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Prepaid_Spend_AmortizationType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Wrapper Element that includes Prepaid Spend Amortization Instance and Data</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Prepaid_Spend_Amortization_Reference" type="wd:Unique_IdentifierObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to an existing Prepaid Spend Amortization</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Prepaid_Spend_Amortization_Data" type="wd:Prepaid_Spend_Amortization_DataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Prepaid_Spend_Amortization_Response_DataType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Wrapper Element that includes Prepaid Spend Amortization Instance and Data</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Prepaid_Spend_Amortization" type="wd:Prepaid_Spend_AmortizationType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Prepaid Spend Amortization</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Get_Prepaid_Spend_Amortizations_ResponseType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Element containing Prepaid Spend Amortization response elements including received criteria, references, data based on criteria and grouping, results filter and result summary</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Request_Criteria" type="wd:Prepaid_Spend_Amortization_Request_CriteriaType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Get Prepaid Spend Amortization Request Critiera</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Response_Filter" type="wd:Response_FilterType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Get Prepaid Spend Amortization Response Filter</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Response_Group" type="wd:Prepaid_Spend_Amortization_Response_GroupType" minOccurs="0"/>
<xsd:element name="Response_Results" type="wd:Response_ResultsType" minOccurs="0"/>
<xsd:element name="Response_Data" type="wd:Prepaid_Spend_Amortization_Response_DataType" minOccurs="0"/>
</xsd:sequence>
<xsd:attribute ref="wd:version"/>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Prepaid_Spend_Amortization_DataType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Element containing all Prepaid Spend Amortization data</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Accounting_Date" type="xsd:date" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Accounting Date of the Prepaid Spend Amotization</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Supplier_Invoice_Reference" type="wd:Supplier_InvoiceObjectType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to an existing Supplier Invoice for the Prepaid Spend Amortization</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>To Submit Prepaid Spend Amortization, the referenced Supplier Invoice must be approved, paid, prepaid option true and a manual release type.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Submit_Prepaid_Spend_Amortization_RequestType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Element containing Prepaid Spend Amortization Business Processing Options and all Prepaid Spend Amortization data items required to submit a Prepaid Spend Amortization</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Business_Process_Parameters" type="wd:Financials_Business_Process_ParametersType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Business Process Parameters provide the ability to auto-submit to the business process.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Prepaid_Spend_Amortization_Data" type="wd:Prepaid_Spend_Amortization_DataType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Prepaid Spend Amortization Data</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
<xsd:attribute ref="wd:version"/>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Submit_Prepaid_Spend_Amortization_ResponseType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Prepaid Spend Amortization Reference</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Prepaid_Spend_Amortization_Reference" type="wd:Unique_IdentifierObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to an existing Prepaid Spend Amortization</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
<xsd:attribute ref="wd:version"/>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Supplier_Invoice_Schedule_DataType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Element containing Supplier Invoice Schedule Data</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Only Distribution Method of "CUSTOM" is currently allowed for Supplier Contract type Schedules.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Day of Month can only be selected with Monthly, Quarterly, or Yearly frequencies.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Contract Type does not allow Receipts therefore you cannot select the Receipt Date Option.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Contract does not have a Signed Date therefore you cannot select the Contract Signed Date Option.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>A From Date must be entered when the Date Option is Use From Date.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>A To Date must be entered when the Date Option is Use To Date.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>When Schedule Method is not Custom, then Schedule From Date and either Number of Installments or To Date are required.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Billing Frequency is required unless Billing Method is Custom.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>End Date can't be before the date of completed installments or installments in progress.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Frequency Behavior can't be changed with already completed Installments.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Schedule Number of Installments can't be less than the number of Installments already completed or in progress.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Schedule Start Date can't be changed with completed installments.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>In Order to use "Automatically submit schedules" you must also use "Automatically regenerate installments".</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>"Automatically regenerate installments" may only be used with Spread Even Distribution Type.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You must submit at least one contract line.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>At Least one Supplier Contract Line provided is used by a different Supplier Contract Schedule. Each Supplier Contract Line may only be used by a single Supplier Contract Schedule.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Supplier Contract Lines must be for the same Supplier Contract.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You may provide either a Date Option Reference or a Day of the Month but not both.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You may provide either the Number of Installments or the To Date but not both.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Either a Date Option or a Day of Month is required if Distribution Method is not Custom.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Supplier Contract Lines provided are for a Supplier Contract that does not allow Supplier Invoice Schedules.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Invoice Class must be active, have supplier accounts usage, and be for the same country as the company on this document.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You cannot specify a Withholding tax code in the transaction tax code reference</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't specify a third party tax code in the transaction tax code reference.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Supplier_Invoice_Schedule_ID" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Supplier Invoice Schedule Reference ID. This is the Supplier Invoice Schedule unique identifier.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Submit" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Submit flag. The service will attempt to submit the schedule if this is on.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Schedule_Status_Reference" type="wd:Document_StatusObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to an existing Schedule Status</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Company_Reference" type="wd:CompanyObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference element representing the schedule company.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Company provided does not match the Supplier Contract Company from the Supplier Contract Lines provided.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Supplier_Reference" type="wd:Resource_ProviderObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference element representing the schedule supplier.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:choice>
<xsd:element name="Supplier_Connection_Reference" type="wd:Remit-To_Supplier_ConnectionObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to an existing Supplier Business Connection.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Supplier Connection is not valid for Supplier.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Supplier Invoice override payment type is not an acceptable payment for Supplier Connection.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Supplier Connection is Inactive.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Use_Default_Supplier_Connection" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>TRUE or FALSEIf this is set to 'TRUE' the default supplier connection will be derived.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:choice>
<xsd:element name="Currency_Reference" type="wd:CurrencyObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference element representing the schedule currency.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Currency provided does not match the Supplier Contract Currency from the Supplier Contract Lines provided.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Statutory_Invoice_Type_Reference" type="wd:Invoice_TypeObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Statutory Invoice Type for Supplier Invoice Schedule.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Supplier_Contract_Reference" type="wd:Supplier_ContractObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference element representing the schedule supplier contract.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Common_Reference_ID_Type>Supplier_Contract_ID</wd:Common_Reference_ID_Type>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Supplier Contract provided does not match the Supplier Contract from the Supplier Contract Lines provided.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Supplier_Contract_Lines_Reference" type="wd:Installment_ItemObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>This is a reference to an existing Supplier Contract Line that isn't used by another Supplier Contract type Schedule.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Schedule_Description" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Schedule Description.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Schedule_On_Hold" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Schedule On Hold flag.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Tax_Code_Reference" type="wd:Tax_CodeObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Default Tax Code Reference</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>You can't specify a third party tax code in the transaction tax code reference.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't specify a third party tax code in the transaction tax code reference.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>You can't submit a Tax Code when the Company has a third party tax integration enabled for Supplier Invoices.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't submit a Tax Code when the Company has a third party tax integration enabled for Supplier Invoices.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Payment_Terms_Reference" type="wd:Payment_TermsObjectType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference element representing a unique instance of Payment Terms.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Override_Payment_Type_Reference" type="wd:Payment_TypeObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to the override Supplier Invoice Payment Type.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Separate_Payment" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Separate Payment</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Auto-submit_for_Approval" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Auto-Submit Invoices for Approval flag.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Supplier_Invoice_Reference_Number" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Supplier Invoice Reference Number</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Distribution_Method_Reference" type="wd:Schedule_Distribution_MethodObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to the Supplier Contract type Schedule Distribution Method. Valid values are: - Custom (CUSTOM). - Defined Installment (RECURRING). - Spread Even (EVEN).</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Distribute_by_Quantity" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Distribute by Quantity Flag. Use this flag to distribute the Schedule Installments by Quantity instead of by Amount.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Frequency__Reference" type="wd:Frequency_BehaviorObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference element representing the schedule Installment Frequency.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="From_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>From date. The system generates installments based on this value.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="To_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>To date. The system generates installments based on this value.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Number_of_Installments" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Number of installments. The system generates installments based on this value.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Either a To Date or a Number of Installments is required if Distribution Method is not Custom.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="12"/>
<xsd:minInclusive value="0"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="0"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Date_Option_Reference" type="wd:Procurement_Date_OptionObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to the Date Option used for Installment generation. Valid values are: - Contract Line Start Date (LINE_START). - Contract Signed Date (CONTRACT_SIGNED). - Contract Start Date (CONTRACT_START). - Receipt Date (RECEIPT). - Use From Date (SCHEDULE_FROM_DATE). - Use To Date (SCHEDULE_TO_DATE).</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>None of the Contract Lines selected have a Start Date therefore you cannot select the Contract Line Start Date Option.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Day_of_Month" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Day of Month. The system generates installments based on this value.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="12"/>
<xsd:minInclusive value="0"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="0"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Automatically_Regenerate_Installments" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Automatically Regenerate Installments Flag. Use this flag to Regenerate installments when Supplier Contract Amendments are completed.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Automatically_Submit_Schedules" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Automatically Submit Schedules Flag. Use this flag when automatically regenerating installments when Supplier Contract Amendments are completed to automatically submit the Supplier Contract type Schedule.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="System_Generated" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the Supplier Invoice Schedule was System Generated. Not enterable for Submit Supplier Invoice Schedule web service. It is used only by Get Supplier Invoice Schedule web service.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>System Generated can't be changed. Used only for Get Web Services.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Supplier_Invoice_Installment_Replacement_Data" type="wd:Supplier_Invoice_Installment_Replacement_DataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Supplier_Invoice_Installment_Replacement_DataType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Element containing Supplier Invoice Installment Data</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>You may not update installments with status Canceled, Completed, or In Progress.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Cannot update an installment if its status is Canceled, Completed, or In Progress.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Supplier Invoice Installment Line Data is required.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Please select "Use Installment Overrides" flag if you wish to override the Tax Code, Payment Terms, Supplier Invoice Payment Type or Memo.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>When creating a new Installment, please provide a unique Installment Number. If updating an existing Installment Please provide an Installment Number, an Installment ID or an Installment Reference.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>You can't specify a third party tax code in the transaction tax code reference.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't specify a third party tax code in the transaction tax code reference.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Supplier_Invoice_Installment_ID" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Supplier Invoice Installment Reference ID. This is the Supplier Invoice Installment unique identifier.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Supplier_Invoice_Installment_Reference" type="wd:Supplier_Invoice_InstallmentObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to an existing Supplier Invoice Installment.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Installment_Number" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Installment Number for Schedule.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="12"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="0"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Status_Reference" type="wd:Document_StatusObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Installment status</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Invoice_Date" type="xsd:date" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Installment Date. This will be the Supplier Invoice Date for the Installment.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="From_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Installment From date</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="To_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Installment To date</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Supplier_Invoice_Reference" type="wd:Supplier_InvoiceObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A reference to the Supplier Invoice created from this Installment. This field is Read Only.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="On_Hold" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Installment On Hold flag</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Use_Installment_Overrides" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Override Line flag. Use this to specify values on the installment line instead of using values derived from either the installment, the schedule, or the contract line. This must be on to specify overrides.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Tax_Code_Reference" type="wd:Tax_CodeObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to an existing Tax Code to be use as an override.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>You can't submit a Tax Code when the Company has a third party tax integration enabled for Supplier Invoices.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't submit a Tax Code when the Company has a third party tax integration enabled for Supplier Invoices.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Payment_Terms_Reference" type="wd:Payment_TermsObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to an existing Payment Terms to be use as an override.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Payment_Type_Reference" type="wd:Payment_TypeObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to an existing Payment Type to be use as an override.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Memo" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Override Installment Memo</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Supplier_Invoice_Installment_Line_Data" type="wd:Supplier_Contract_Installment_Line_DataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Supplier_Contract_Installment_Line_DataType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Element containing Supplier Invoice Schedule Installment Line data</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Please Select "Use Line Overrides" if you wish to override the Unit Of Measure, Line description or Worktags.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Supplier Contract Line may only be used once per Installment.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Supplier_Contract_Line_Reference" type="wd:Supplier_Contract_LineObjectType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>This is a reference to an existing Supplier Contract Line that isn't used by another Supplier Contract type Schedule.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Supplier Contract Line on Installment must be in the list of Supplier Contract Lines specified for the Schedule.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Service lines are not allowed for the provided Supplier Contract Type</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Line_Order" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Line order</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Use_Line_Overrides" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Override Line flag. Use this to specify values on the installment line instead of using values derived from either the installment, the schedule, or the contract line. This must be on to specify overrides.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Quantity" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Quantity. If you supply this value as an override, you must also enable the Override Line flag.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You may not specify a Quantity for this installment if you are not distributing Installments by Quantity.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Although Supplier Invoice Schedules may distribute installments by Amount or Quantity, Purchase Order Schedules always distribute by Quantity.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Quantity is required when distributing by Quantity.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Quantity distribution is not allowed for Service Lines.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="22"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="2"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Unit_Cost" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Installment Line Unit Cost. If you supply this value as an override, you must also enable the Override Line flag. The Unit Cost can only be entered for Supplier Invoice Schedules distributed by Amount.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Unit Cost may only be provided on Schedules using the Custom Distribution Method.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Unit Cost is not allowed for Service Line.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="From_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>From Date. If you supply this value as an override, you must also enable the Override Line flag.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="To_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>To Date. If you supply this value as an override, you must also enable the Override Line flag.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Payment_Amount" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The total amount minus the retention amount. This field is for returning values only. Any values entered will be ignored.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Total_Amount" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Installment Line Amount</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You may not specify an amount when distributing by quantity.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Retention_Amount" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The amount to retain from the scheduled supplier invoice installment.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Retention amount is only allowed for supplier contract lines that are subject to retention</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Retention Amount can not be more than Installment Line Amount</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="18"/>
<xsd:minInclusive value="0"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="3"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Unit_of_Measure_Reference" type="wd:Unit_of_MeasureObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to an existing Unit of Measure. If you supply this value as an override, you must also enable the Override Line flag.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Unit of measure is not allowed for Service Line.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Line_Description" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Installment Line Description from Supplier Contract type Installment Line or from Supplier Contract Line.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Spend_Category_Reference" type="wd:Accounting_CategoryObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to an existing Spend Category</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Worktags_Reference" type="wd:Accounting_WorktagObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Worktags from Override or from Supplier Contract Line.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The following Accounting Worktag types are invalid: [invalid].</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The following Accounting Worktags are required but have not been assigned: [missing].</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The following Accounting Worktag types are invalid: [invalid].</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The following Accounting Worktags are required but have not been assigned: [missing].</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>[invalid worktag value message]</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Submit_Supplier_Invoice_Schedule_RequestType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Submit Supplier Invoice Schedule Request.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>The Web Service is set to Add Only; documents cannot be resubmitted.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Web Service is set to Add Only; documents cannot be resubmitted.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Supplier_Invoice_Schedule_Reference" type="wd:Supplier_Invoice_ScheduleObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to an existing Supplier Invoice Schedule</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Business_Process_Parameters" type="wd:Financials_Business_Process_ParametersType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
<xsd:element name="Supplier_Invoice_Schedule_Data" type="wd:Supplier_Invoice_Schedule_DataType" minOccurs="0"/>
</xsd:sequence>
<xsd:attribute name="Add_Only" type="xsd:boolean">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Add Only Flag. Indicates that the service is an add only, not an update. If an existing instance is found and this flag is set there will be an error.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:attribute>
<xsd:attribute ref="wd:version"/>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Submit_Supplier_Invoice_Schedule_ResponseType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Submit Supplier Invoice Schedule Response</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Supplier_Invoice_Schedule_Reference" type="wd:Supplier_Invoice_ScheduleObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to an existing Supplier Invoice Schedule</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
<xsd:attribute ref="wd:version"/>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Suspend_Asset_Depreciation_RequestType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Element containing data needed to suspend asset depreciation</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Suspend_Asset_Depreciation_Data" type="wd:Suspend_Asset_Depreciation_for_WWS_DataType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Contains the items needed to suspend asset depreciation.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
<xsd:attribute ref="wd:version"/>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Suspend_Asset_Depreciation_for_WWS_DataType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Element containing Business Asset data to suspend an asset</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Suspend date is EARLIER than depreciation start date of an existing cost or useful life adjustment</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Suspend date cannot be earlier than in service date or an existing resume date</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>In progress events for the asset need to be resolved before suspending the depreciation</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Depreciation may not be suspended for an asset that has an invalid document status of Disposed, Out of Service or Removed</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Discrete Composite Asset or Components of Non-Discrete Composite Asset cannot be suspended.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>The book selected is not a configured book for this company</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The book selected is not a configured book for this company</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Suspend date cannot be after last depreciation period end date</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Suspend date cannot be after last depreciation period end date</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Suspend date cannot be prior to depreciation start date</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Suspend date cannot be prior to depreciation start date</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>You cannot suspend depreciation in an asset book that is already suspended.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You cannot suspend depreciation in an asset book that is already suspended.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Depreciation has been posted or accounted for periods affected by suspend date</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Reference" type="wd:Business_AssetObjectType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The Asset one would like to suspend depreciation for.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>The asset is part of a lease contract. You can't suspend depreciation on leased assets.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The asset is part of a lease contract. You can't suspend depreciation on leased assets.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't suspend depreciation on an asset with a contract information.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Suspend_From_Date" type="xsd:date" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Suspend depreciation on or after this date is required for ALL requests. The response will contain the ‘Suspend From Date’ from the latest suspend schedule.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Fiscal period must exist for the suspend from date</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Suspend_To_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Suspend depreciation on or before this date is required for ALL requests. The response will contain the ‘Suspend To Date’ from the latest suspend schedule.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Fiscal period must exist for the suspend to date</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Suspend To Date cannot be prior to Suspend From Date.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Suspend To Date cannot be after depreciation end date (contract end date).</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Suspend To Date cannot be used if asset has no depreciation end date (contract end date)</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Suspend To Date is required for assets related to a contract and if the asset is not contract-related, Suspend To Date should not be passed in the request.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Restricted_To_Books_Reference" type="wd:Asset_BookObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The Asset Book(s) to record the asset depreciation.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Suspend_Asset_Depreciation_ResponseType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Returns the asset that had its depreciation suspended.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Asset_Reference" type="wd:Business_AssetObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Returns the asset that had its depreciation suspended.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
<xsd:attribute ref="wd:version"/>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Bill_To_Address_ReferenceType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Contains a reference instance or a Address Reference ID for an existing address</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Provided Bill To Address is Invalid for this Purchase Order</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Provided Bill To Address is Invalid for this Purchase Order</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
