<xsd:documentation>You selected an invalid supplier contract for this supplier invoice. Select a supplier contract that's valid for the company, supplier, and document date; not undergoing an amendment; and supports manual supplier invoices.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You selected an invalid supplier contract for this supplier invoice. Select a supplier contract that's valid for the company, supplier, and document date; not undergoing an amendment; and supports manual supplier invoices.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Specify a value for either Remit-To Supplier Connection or Use Default Supplier Connection.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Specify a value for either Remit-To Supplier Connection or Use Default Supplier Connection.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>The alternate ledger currency override you entered must be unique. Enter a unique override currency.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You entered duplicate currency rate details for currency, [currency]. Enter a unique currency.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Enter the currency conversion rate to apply between the transaction currency [Transaction Currency] and the alternate ledger currency of the following company ledgers: [Ledgers]</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>You need to enable a payment purpose code during tenant set up to add a payment purpose code to the invoice or adjustment</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You need to enable a payment purpose code during tenant set up to add a payment purpose code to the invoice or adjustment</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You entered a receiving payment purpose code that is not marked as Active. You must enter the receiving payment purpose code as Active.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You entered an originating payment purpose code that is not marked as Active. You must enter the originating payment purpose code as Active.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You entered a payment purpose code that is not marked Receiving.You must enter the receiving purpose of the payment as Receiving.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You entered a payment purpose code that is not marked Originating.You must enter the originating purpose of the payment as Originating.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't enter a purchase order reference if it is not a down payment invoice.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't add retention details for a down payment invoice.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Down payment terms must be entered in purchase order to create down payment invoice.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't enter values in these fields for down payment invoices: Freight Amount, Other Charges, Worktag Split template, Tax only flag, Default Witholding Tax Code, Witholding Tax Amount, Supplier Contract Reference.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't add prepaid details for a down payment invoice.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>The Down Payment invoice company, supplier, and currency must match the ones on the purchase order.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Down Payment invoice company, supplier, and currency must match the ones on the purchase order.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't specify down payment invoices when the down payment flag is selected.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Enter a discount date override with a date that is later than the invoice date.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't resubmit the supplier invoice because 1 or more projects have billable line status of billed, ready to bill, or revenue recognized.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't create a down payment invoice for a purchase order that's fully invoiced.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't create a down payment invoice if you have worktag balancing enabled.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>You can't enter a default tax option for a down payment invoice with a company that has third party tax enabled.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't enter a default tax option for a down payment invoice with a company that has third party tax enabled.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't enter values in these fields for down payment invoices: Freight Amount, Other Charges, Worktag Split template, Tax only flag, Default Witholding Tax Code, Witholding Tax Amount, Supplier Contract Reference.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't submit an invoice with the fields : [field]. These fields are hidden fields. Use the Configure Optional Field task to unhide these fields.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't submit an invoice without the fields : [field]. These fields are required fields. Use the Configure Optional Field task to make these not required fields.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The bill-from and ship-from addresses on the supplier invoice aren't enabled for this company: [Company]. On the Edit Supplier Account Options task, select the Enable Bill-From and Ship-From Address for the Supplier Invoice Document check box to enter the bill from or ship-from address</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The bill-from address is not associated with a usage type of Billing. Add the usage type of Billing to this bill-from address.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The ship-from address is not associated with a usage type of Shipping. Add the usage type of Shipping to this ship-from address.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>You can't specify a third party tax code in the withholding tax code reference. Specify a non third party withholding tax code.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't specify a third party tax code in the withholding tax code reference. Specify a non third party withholding tax code.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Set Amount Inclusive of Tax as false. The specified company hasn't configured a third party tax service to accept an amount inclusive of tax as the extended amount.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>You can't specify values for Supplier Invoice Line Third Party Tax Rate Data or Supplier Invoice Line Third Party Withholding Tax Rate Data for this document type. Workday doesn't support third-party tax calculations for this document type.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't specify values for Supplier Invoice Line Third Party Tax Rate Data or Supplier Invoice Line Third Party Withholding Tax Rate Data for this document type. Workday doesn't support third-party tax calculations for this document type.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Do not set Amount Inclusive of Tax as true when the invoice has a retention amount.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Specify an active bank routing code that's mapped to a bank account in the bank routing rules. This bank routing code is either not active or invalid:[Bank Routing Code]</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Specify either Is Down Payment or Landed Costs in Tax.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Specify either Tax Only or Landed Costs in Tax.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Specify either Amount Inclusive of Tax or Landed Costs in Tax.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Supplier_Invoice_ID" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Supplier Invoice ID. This is the Supplier Invoice unique identifier</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Invalid ID value.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Submit" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Submit for Approval is a boolean flag indicating if the transaction is to be submitted or saved in draft mode. If this flag is set, the transaction will be submitted, otherwise the transaction is saved in draft.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Locked_in_Workday" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Set to True to disable editing and canceling the invoice inside the Workday application. Invoice can only be updated from the web service.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Invoice_Number" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>If adding a new invoice, then make the Invoice Number the same value as Reference ID. If updating an existing invoice, then make it the same value as the Reference ID of that invoice. If you do not make the Invoice Number the same as Reference ID, then duplicate Invoice Numbers for different invoices may be created. The Reference ID is the only value checked as a unique identifier. Note that the name of the Reference ID is different for each invoice type: e.g. Supplier Invoice ID, Supplier Invoice Adjustment ID, Customer Invoice Adjustment ID, and Customer Invoice ID.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="External_Supplier_Invoice_Source_Reference" type="wd:External_Transaction_Source__All_ObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The External Supplier Invoice Source. Defaults to Web Service, but you can override it.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Enter Web Service or an external supplier invoice source that isn't a Workday-owned value.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Enter an active External Supplier Invoice Source.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Leave blank or enter the same External Supplier Invoice Source from the supplier invoice document.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Company_Reference" type="wd:CompanyObjectType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>This is the company that tranasction is for. This is the reference id value of the company.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Common_Reference_ID_Type>Company_Reference_ID</wd:Common_Reference_ID_Type>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Payment_Practices" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Payment Practice field to flag a Supplier Invoice for Payment Practices Reporting</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Currency_Reference" type="wd:CurrencyObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>This is the reference id of currency of the transaction If no currency is specified, Workday will first look to see if the payer/payee has a preferred currency and if not, currency will be populated with the company base currency. If the company base currency is not allowed currency for payer/payee then transaction will not be able to be submitted for approval.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Common_Reference_ID_Type>Currency_ID</wd:Common_Reference_ID_Type>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Currency entered is not listed as an Accepted Currency by Supplier.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Currency entered is not listed as an Accepted Currency by Supplier.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Enter a Currency. The Supplier, Company, or Remit to Connection don't have a default currency.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Enter a Currency. The Supplier, Company, or Remit to Connection don't have a default currency.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:choice>
<xsd:element name="Supplier_Reference" type="wd:SupplierObjectType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Supplier Reference is the reference to the Supplier the invoice is from.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Common_Reference_ID_Type>Supplier_ID</wd:Common_Reference_ID_Type>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Select a Supplier that is active or on hold to create the supplier invoice.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Contingent_Worker_Reference" type="wd:Contingent_WorkerObjectType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to an existing Contingent Worker</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:choice>
<xsd:element name="Supplier_Connection_Reference" type="wd:Remit-To_Supplier_ConnectionObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to an existing Supplier Business Connection.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Supplier Connection is Inactive.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Supplier Invoice override payment type is not an acceptable payment for Supplier Connection.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Supplier Connection is not valid for Supplier.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Use_Default_Supplier_Connection" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>TRUE or FALSEIf this is set to 'TRUE' the default supplier connection will be derived.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Default_Tax_Option_Reference" type="wd:Tax_OptionObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to an existing Tax Option. If left blank, will default from the Company.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Ship-To_Address_Reference" type="wd:Unique_IdentifierObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to an existing Ship-To address.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Ship-To_Address_ID_Reference" type="wd:Address_ReferenceObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>We update these web services to enable you to submit a ship-to address using the Address Reference ID field:* Import Supplier Invoice* Submit Supplier Invoice</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Bill-From_Address_Reference" type="wd:Address_ReferenceObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to an existing Bill-From address.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The address [address] is invalid for the supplier: [supplier]. Use the supplier change configuration to add a valid billing address for this supplier.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Ship-From_Address_Reference" type="wd:Address_ReferenceObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to an existing Ship-From address.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The address [address] is invalid for the supplier: [supplier]. Use the supplier change configuration to add a valid shipping address for this supplier.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Tax_Code_Reference" type="wd:Tax_CodeObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>This is the reference id value of the tax code. If not submitted, Workday will use the payee default the tax code.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>You can't submit a Tax Code at the header when the Company has a third party tax integration enabled for Supplier Invoices.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't submit a Tax Code at the header when the Company has a third party tax integration enabled for Supplier Invoices.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Default_Withholding_Tax_Code_Reference" type="wd:Tax_CodeObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>This is the reference id value of the default withholding tax code. If not submitted, Workday will use the payee default the withholding tax code.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Invoice_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Format is MM/DD/YYYY.If this is left blank, Workday will populate invoice date with the current date.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Invoice_Received_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Field to store the Invoice Received Date value</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Invoice_Delivery_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Enter Invoice Delivery Date</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Invoice_Billing_Start_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Enter Invoice Billing Start Date</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Invoice_Billing_End_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Enter Invoice Billing End Date</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Invoice Billing End Date must be greater than or equal to the Invoice Billing Start Date.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Discount_Amount_Override" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Overrides calculated payment discounts.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't use the Discount Amount Override field because it is a hidden field. Use the Configure Optional Fields task to unhide the Discount Amount Override field before you use the Discount Amount Override field for web services.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Discount_Date_Override" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Overrides default discount date.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't enter a discount date override when there is no discount amount override or discount payment terms. Enter a discount amount override, discount payment terms, or both before you enter the discount date override.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Enter a discount date override with a date that is earlier than the invoice due date or the due date override, if an override exists.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't use the Discount Date Override field because it is a hidden field. Use the Configure Optional Fields task to unhide the Discount Date Override field before you use the Discount Date Override field for web services.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Due_Date_Override" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Format is MM/DD/YYYY.If a date is provided, it will override the due date that Workday automatically determines based on the invoice date and payment terms.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Due Date must not be earlier than Invoice Date</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Due Date must not be earlier than Invoice Date</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Separate_Payment" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Separate Payment</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Accounting_Date_Override" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Override date for Accounting.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Budget_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Use this field to override the Budget Date on all supplier invoice lines and splits.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="On_Hold" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>TRUE or FALSEIf this is set to 'TRUE' the invoice will be put on hold.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Hold_Reason_Reference" type="wd:Supplier_Invoice_Hold_ReasonObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>This is the reference for Supplier Invoice Hold Reason</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't add a hold reason to an invoice that is not on-hold.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The supplier invoice hold reason is inactive.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Control_Amount_Total" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>This is the expected invoice total including tax. It is optional. An invoice cannot be submittted for approval if it has a non-zero control total that does not equal the sum of the extended amount for all invoice lines plus tax.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Tax_Amount" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Tax Amount</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>You can only enter a tax amount in the header if you select Enter Tax Due to Supplier as the tax option.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can only enter a tax amount in the header if you select Enter Tax Due to Supplier as the tax option.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Freight_Amount" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Freight Amount</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Other_Charges" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Other Charges</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Landed_Costs_in_Tax" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>When true Landed Costs are included in tax calculations for a Supplier Invoice</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Worktag_Split_Template_Reference" type="wd:Worktag_Split_TemplateObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Worktag Split Allocation Template for Supplier Invoice</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Enter a valid company. This company is not valid for the Worktag Split template: [WST]</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Enter an active Worktag Split Template. This Worktag Split Template is inactive: [WST].</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Enter a different Worktag Split Template or Invoice Date. This Worktag Split Template [template] doesn't have splits for the date [effectivedate].</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Tax_Only" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Tax Only Boolean to indicate if the Supplier Invoice is Tax Only</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Amount_Inclusive_of_Tax" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>If true, the value specified for Extended Amount is the amount inclusive of tax.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Do not set Amount Inclusive of Tax as true when the invoice is a down payment invoice or references a down payment invoice.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Down_Payment" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Down Payment</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Don't specify a discount override date or discount override amount for a down payment invoice.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Down_Payment_Purchase_Order_Reference" type="wd:Purchase_OrderObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The Purchase Order for this Down Payment</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Referenced_Invoices_Reference" type="wd:Supplier_InvoiceObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Tax Only invoice Workset for adding Referenced Invoices</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Supplier_Document_Received" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Boolean attribute indicating if the Supplier Paper Document was received (possibly through mail or fax) . If this is set then a Supplier Reference is required that will provide information for locating that document.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Suppliers_Invoice_Number" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Free form text field to provide a Supplier Reference memo. The Supplier Reference is not a Workday Reference ID, but a text field for providing additional information about the Supplier Invoice.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>The Supplier Reference entered has already been used on another invoice or adjustment for this supplier</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Supplier Reference entered has already been used on another invoice or adjustment for this supplier</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>If Supplier Document Received is true, a Supplier Reference Number must also be submitted.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>If Supplier Document Received is true, a Supplier Reference Number must also be submitted.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="External_PO_Number" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Free form text field for providing addition information on the Purchase Order that the Supplier Invoice is for. This is not a Workday Purchase Order Reference ID.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Statutory_Invoice_Type_Reference" type="wd:Invoice_TypeObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Invoice Type for Supplier Invoice.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Supplier_Contract_Reference" type="wd:Supplier_Contract_BaseObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to an existing Supplier Contract</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>The Supplier Contract selected must be for the Supplier on the invoice.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Supplier Contract selected must be for the Supplier on the invoice.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Supplier Contract referenced cannot be an Amendment or History.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Supplier Contract referenced cannot be an Amendment or History.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Document_Link" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Link to a scanned image of the paper invoice</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Memo" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>This transaction header memo will print on the delivered transaction. It is optional freeform text</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Approver_Reference" type="wd:WorkerObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The Approver for Supplier Invoice</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Payment_Terms_Reference" type="wd:Payment_TermsObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>This is the reference id of the payment terms for the invoice. Payment Terms are the rules for establishing when a invoice payment is due and whether discounts are eligible to be taken or given for early payment. This is a required field, but if no payment terms are specified, Workday will populate this with the customer's default payment terms if one is defined. Workday will automatically determine the due date and discount date based on the invoice date and payment terms.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Enter Payment Terms. You can also select a Remit to Connection or Supplier that already has default payment terms configured.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Enter Payment Terms. You can also select a Remit to Connection or Supplier that already has default payment terms configured.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Override_Payment_Type_Reference" type="wd:Payment_TypeObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>A reference to a Payment Type. If one is provided, it will be used in processing the Payment instead of the Supplier's default payment type.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>If Override Payment Type is provided, it must be one of the accepted Payment Types for the Supplier provided.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>If Override Payment Type is provided, it must be one of the accepted Payment Types for the Supplier provided.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Override Payment Type cannot be used if a Supplier is not provided.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Override Payment Type cannot be used if a Supplier is not provided.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Additional_Type_Reference" type="wd:Additional_Reference_TypeObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Additional Type Reference</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Reference_Number" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference Number</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:string">
<xsd:maxLength value="140"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Originating_Country_Payment_Purpose_Reference" type="wd:Payment_Purpose_CodeObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Originating Country Payment Purpose Code. This code is used to identify the purpose of the payment from the originating country.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Receiving_Country_Payment_Purpose_Reference" type="wd:Payment_Purpose_CodeObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Receiving Country Payment Purpose Code. This code is used to identify the purpose of the payment from the receiving country.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Bank_Routing_Code_Reference" type="wd:Bank_Routing_CodeObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>This is the Bank Routing Code for the transaction.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Handling_Code_Reference" type="wd:Payment_Handling_InstructionObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>This is the reference code of the payment handling instructions for the supplier invoice or supplier invoice adjustment.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Prepaid" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Set the Prepaid value to true for Prepaid Invoices where all lines are Prepaid. If set, the lines cannot be also set to Prepaid individually.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Prepayment_Release_Type_Reference" type="wd:Prepaid_Amortization_TypeObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to an existing Prepaid Amortization Type</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Release_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Prepaid Amortization Date</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Expected Amortization Date must be after the Invoice date and the current date.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Expected Amortization Date must be after the Invoice date and the current date.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Frequency_Reference" type="wd:Frequency_BehaviorObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The Frequency to be used when generating the next prepaid accounting entry.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Frequency entered is not a valid value.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Number_of_Installments" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The Number of Installments to use when accounting for the Prepaid Amortization.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="12"/>
<xsd:minInclusive value="0"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="0"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Use_Invoice_Date" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Use the Invoice Date as the starting date for the first installment.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Both the Use Invoice Date and Specified Date cannot be specified at the same time.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Both the Use Invoice Date and Specified Date cannot be specified at the same time.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="From_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Use the Specified Date as the starting date for the first installment.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Retention_Memo" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The retention memo.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Down_Payment_Application_Data" type="wd:Down_Payment_Application_DataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Encapsulates Data Pertaining to a Down Payment being applied</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Additional_Fields_Data_Reference" type="wd:Configurable_Attributes_DataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Encapsulating element containing additional fields data</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Specify a unique Configurable Attribute Reference. You can't use the same Configurable Attribute Reference more than once.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Currency_Rate_Data" type="wd:Currency_Rate_DataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
<xsd:element name="Attachment_Data" type="wd:Financials_Attachment_DataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Attachment Data</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Tax_Code_Data" type="wd:Taxable_Code_Application_DataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Tax Data by Tax Authority and Tax Code. For Customer Invoice Documents and Cash Sales tax data will always be calculated from the line data regardless of what is populated in Tax Rate Application Data. For Purchase Orders, Supplier Invoice Documents and Ad hoc Payments, if data is in Tax Rate Application Data, then that will be the tax information that is saved. Otherwise, the tax will be calculated from the lines.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Invoice_Line_Replacement_Data" type="wd:Supplier_Invoice_Line_Replacement__HV__DataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Supplier Invoice Line Data. A Supplier Invoice may have multiple lines.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Retention_Release_Line_Data" type="wd:Supplier_Invoice_Retention_Release_Line_WWS_DataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Encapsulating element containing Supplier Invoice Retention Release Line data.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Supplier_Invoice_Intercompany_Sub_Process" type="wd:Supplier_Invoice_Intercompany_Sub_ProcessType" minOccurs="0"/>
<xsd:element name="Supplier_Invoice_Prepaid_Amortization_Schedule" type="wd:Supplier_Invoice_Prepaid_Amortization_Schedule_WWS_DataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Prepaid Supplier Invoice Lines for Amortization Schedule</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Work_Queue_Information_Data" type="wd:Supplier_Invoice_Work_Queue_Information_DataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
