</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Supplier Contract Line supplier is On Hold and may not be used.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Supplier Contract Line has been Canceled and cannot be used.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Item is from a Supplier Contract that does not accept Manual Purchase Orders.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Item is from a Supplier Contract that does not accept Manual Purchase Orders.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The sum of the extended amounts on the split lines ([split amt]) must equal the extended amount of the summary line: [amt]</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Please specify an Item or an Item Description.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Please specify an Item or an Item Description.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Please specify an Item or a Spend Category.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Please specify an Item or a Spend Category.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Item Reference on the Item Order Line does not match the Procurement Item on the Supplier Contract Line.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Can not have any combination of Project, Project Phase or Project Task worktags for the same line.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Only one worktag for each type is allowed for each document line.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The End Date must be on or after the Start Date</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Supplier Contract Line Reference for this Service Order Line is not for a Service line.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Catalog items are not allowed on Service Lines.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Deliver-To Location is invalid for the selected Delivery Type and/or Company.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Supplier Contract field is required if there are any Contract Lines referenced.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Extended Amount must be greater than zero if from a Service Contract Line Reference.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Please enter a company that is in the intercompany profile of the company on the purchase order header.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Please Enable Multi-Company on Purchase Orders.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Prepaid, Retention and Due Date aren't supported on Bill Only Purchase Order Service lines.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Spend category "[spend category]" is inactive.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>For Bill Only purchase orders, if there's a Ship-To Address on the line, it must match the header Ship-To Address, otherwise leave it blank on the line. If there is no header Ship-To Address, then the line Ship-To Address must match the company default shipping address.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Enter a valid address for the company on the purchase order line.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Enter the valid spend category '[valid category]' or leave the spend category field blank. This spend category is invalid for service item '[Service Item]': '[Invalid Spend Category]'.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Submit a valid commodity code or leave the commodity code field blank.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Submit a valid commodity code or leave the commodity code field blank. This commodity code isn't set up for the item ‘[Procurement Item]‘: ‘[Invalid Commodity Code]’</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Select only Down Payments or Prepaid, but not both, in the same purchase order line or within the same purchase order.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Select only Down Payments or Prepaid, but not both, in the same purchase order line or within the same purchase order.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Select only Down Payments or Retention, but not both, in the same purchase order line or within the same purchase order.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Select only Down Payments or Retention, but not both, in the same purchase order line or within the same purchase order.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>The Requisition Line referenced is from a Requisition that is Closed or Pending Close.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Requisition Line referenced is from a Requisition that is Closed or Pending Close.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Requisition Line Reference for this Service Order Line must be for a Service Line.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Requisition Line Reference requires a RFQ and can not be sourced to Purchase Order.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Submit approved Requisition Line that is not fully sourced and business process events that are not in progress.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Submit approved Requisition Line that is not fully sourced and business process events that are not in progress.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Company on the Requisition Line Reference for this Purchase Order Line must be a valid company for the Purchase Order.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Extended Amount must be the same sign as the Requisition Line Reference's Extended Amount.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Specify an active worker.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Spend category must have a Spend Category Usage type of Procurement.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Specify an active tax applicability.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Item_Reference" type="wd:Procurement_ItemObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to an existing purchase item. Specifying the purchase item will default values for the Item Description, Spend Category, Tax Applicability, Unit of Measure, and Unit Cost if these options are defined on the purchase item itself.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Common_Reference_ID_Type>Catalog_Item_ID</wd:Common_Reference_ID_Type>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Catalog items are not allowed on Service Lines.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Remove the line or select a different item. You can't submit an item that is Restricted from Purchasing.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Service_Order_Line_ID" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference ID</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Line_Number" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The line number of the Purchase Order.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="4"/>
<xsd:minInclusive value="0"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="0"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Line_Company_Reference" type="wd:CompanyObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The company of the Purchase Order Line.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Description" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Free form text description of the purchase item. The description will default from the item if the description is left blank.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Supplier_Contract_Line_Reference" type="wd:Supplier_Contract_LineObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>An optional reference to an existing Supplier Contract Line in the Workday system. This is used to link the Item Order Line with a Supplier Contract Line.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Supplier Contract specified for the Purchase Order line does not match the Supplier Contract for the Supplier Contract Line: [SC line].</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Supplier Contract specified for the Purchase Order does not match the Supplier Contract for the Supplier Contract Line: [line].</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Commodity_Code_Reference" type="wd:Commodity_CodeObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The commodity code on spend transactions lines. This is a standard code that identifies a type of good or service you order. For example, the United Nations Standard Products and Services Code (UNSPSC) or the National Institute for Governmental Purchasing (NIGP) code. For purchase items and catalog items, you can only submit active commodity codes already associated to the item. For ad hoc based lines, you can submit any active commodity code.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Payment_Status_Reference" type="wd:Document_Payment_StatusObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Payment Status for Purchase Order Line. This field is read-only and ignored on Submit.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Invoice_Status_Reference" type="wd:Document_StatusObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Invoice Status for Purchase Order Line. This field is read-only and ignored on Submit.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Receiving_Status_Reference" type="wd:Document_StatusObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Receiving Status for Purchase Order Line. This field is read-only and ignored on Submit.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Resource_Category_Reference" type="wd:Spend_CategoryObjectType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to the Spend Category. The Spend Category will default from the Purchase Item if the item is specified. This Spend Category must match the Spend Category for the Purchase Item.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Tax_Applicability_Reference" type="wd:Tax_ApplicabilityObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to the Tax Applicability for the Purchase Item. If the item has Tax Code defined, then the Tax Applicability is required.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>Tax Applicability Reference is required is Tax Code is specified.</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Tax Applicability Reference is required.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Tax_Code_Reference" type="wd:Tax_CodeObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to the Tax Code for the Purchase Item. The Tax Code is defaulted from the Purchase Order Data element if one is specified.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Tax Code on the line is only allowed if the Tax Option is Calculate Tax Due to Supplier or Calculate Use Tax.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Tax_Rate_Options_Data" type="wd:Tax_Rate_Options_DataType" minOccurs="0"/>
<xsd:element name="Extended_Amount" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The Extended Amount for the Service Order Line. This value must be the same sign as the Requisition Line Reference or zero, if present, and must be positive if there is a Supplier Contract Line Reference, if present.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="18"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="3"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Due_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The anticipated date by which the Purchase Order Line should be fulfilled.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Start_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Start Date</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="End_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>End Date</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Prepaid" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Prepaid flag at the Line level</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Prepaid Amortization Type is required when the prepaid boolean is set.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Down_Payment" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Down Payment</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Retention" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Retention flag at the Line level</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Budget_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Use this field to override the Budget Date on a purchase order line.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Memo" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Memo for the Purchase Order Line.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Ship_To_Address_Reference" type="wd:Address_ReferenceObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The address where the line item will be shipped to.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Ship_To_Contact_Reference" type="wd:WorkerObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The ship-to contact worker associated to the line item.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Requester_Reference" type="wd:WorkerObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Requester for the Purchase Order Line.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Deliver_To_Location_Reference" type="wd:LocationObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The location where the items will be delivered.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Requisition_Line_Reference" type="wd:Requisition_LineObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The Requisition Line linked to the Purchase Order Line.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Supplier_Contract_Reference" type="wd:Supplier_ContractObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>This field is only enabled for Companies and Tenants which are Opted-In to Consolidate Requisition Lines by Supplier regardless of Supplier Contract.Use this field to assign a specific Supplier Contract to this Spend Line.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Supplier Contract on the Document Line is Closed or Pending Close.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Currency for the Supplier Contract on the Purchase Order Line must match Currency for the Purchase Order.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The Supplier Contract selected on the Document Line must be for the Supplier on the Document Header.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You selected an invalid supplier contract for this purchase order line. Select a supplier contract that's valid for the company, supplier, and document date; not undergoing an amendment; and supports manual purchase orders.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Storage_Location_Reference" type="wd:LocationObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to an existing location for the item.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Worktags_Reference" type="wd:Accounting_WorktagObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to existing worktags. Worktags are a way to mark tasks and business objects to make them easier to access and summarize. Each transaction can include one value for each worktag type and is subject to configurable validation when submitted for approval.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<xsd:documentation>The Worktags provided are not valid for this transaction</xsd:documentation>
<wd:Validation_Message>[list of worktag types] not valid for this transaction.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Worktags are not allowed when there are split lines.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>[not allowed worktag types on Spend Transactions]</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The [type] is/are not available for use with the company/s: [partitionable] [company]</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>[worktag value] is not permitted as an allowed value for worktag type: [worktag type], because it is inactive.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>[missing required worktag types on Spend Transactions]</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Select a balancing worktag for Worktags of the following type: [type]</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The following Accounting Worktags are required but have not been assigned: [missing].</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Enter a company that matches on the award line in effect for grant: [grant]. This company doesn't match the grant on the award line: [comp].</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>[invalid worktag value message]</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Service_Purchase_Order_Line_Split_Data" type="wd:Business_Document_Line_Split_DataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Quantity splits are not allowed for Service Lines.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Close_Status_Reference" type="wd:Document_StatusObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The status of a closed purchase order line. This field is read-only and ignored when you submit.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Close_Status_Information" type="wd:Close_Status_InformationType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Additional information on the status of the closed purchase order (PO) line. Includes information such as the date the PO line was closed, who closed the line, and the reason it was closed. This field is read-only and ignored when you submit.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Get_Request_for_Quote_RequestType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Element containing sub elements for Request Reference, Request Criteria, Response Filter and Response Group for getting Request for Quote data.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:choice>
<xsd:element name="Request_References" type="wd:Request_for_Quote_Request_ReferencesType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The Request for Quote Request References element contains the instances of Request for Quote.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Request_Criteria" type="wd:Request_for_Quote_Request_CriteriaType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>This element content contains the Procurement Card Transaction Verification Request Criteria Element</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:choice>
<xsd:element name="Response_Filter" type="wd:Response_FilterType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Parameters that let you filter the data returned in the response. You can filter returned data by dates and page attributes.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Response_Group" type="wd:Request_for_Quote_Response_GroupType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Element containing Request for Quote Data.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
<xsd:attribute ref="wd:version"/>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Request_for_Quote_Request_ReferencesType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The Request for Quote Request References element contains instances of Request for Quote for get operation.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Request_for_Quote_Reference" type="wd:Request_for_QuoteObjectType" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to an existing Request for Quote.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Request_for_Quote_Request_CriteriaType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The Request for Quote Request Criteria element contains criteria to find Request for Quotes.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Company_Reference" type="wd:CompanyObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Company Reference</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="RFQ_Type_Reference" type="wd:Request_for_Quote_TypeObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Request for Quote Type Reference.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Document_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The date of the Request for Quote.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="RFQ_Start_Date_On_or_After" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Request for Quote Start Date On or After</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="RFQ_Start_Date_On_or_Before" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Request for Quote Start Date On or Before</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="RFQ_End_Date_On_or_After" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Request for Quote End Date On or After</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="RFQ_End_Date_On_or_Before" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Request for Quote End Date On or Before</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Sourcing_Buyer_Reference" type="wd:WorkerObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to Sourcing Buyer of Request for Quote.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="RFQ_Status_Reference" type="wd:Document_StatusObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to the Document Status for the Request for Quote. This field is read-only, and will be ignored on a Put or Submit.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Request_for_Quote_Response_GroupType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Element containing Request for Quote response grouping options.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Include_Reference" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Include Reference</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Include_Attachment_Data" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Flag indicating whether the attachments within Request for Quote Data is to be included in the response.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Get_Request_for_Quote_ResponseType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Element containing Request for Quote response elements including request data and request result data.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Request_References" type="wd:Request_for_Quote_Request_ReferencesType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The Request for Quote Request References element contains the instances of Request for Quote.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Request_Criteria" type="wd:Request_for_Quote_Request_CriteriaType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>This element content contains the Procurement Card Transaction Verification Request Criteria Element</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Response_Filter" type="wd:Response_FilterType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Parameters that let you filter the data returned in the response. You can filter returned data by dates and page attributes.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Response_Group" type="wd:Request_for_Quote_Response_GroupType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>This element content contains the echoed Request for Quote Response Group Element.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Response_Results" type="wd:Response_ResultsType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The "Response_Results" element contains summary information about the data that has been returned from your request including "Total_Results", "Total_Pages", and the current "Page" returned.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Response_Data" type="wd:Request_for_Quote_Response_DataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Element containing Request for Quote Data.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
<xsd:attribute ref="wd:version"/>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Request_for_Quote_Response_DataType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Wrapper element containing Request for Quote response data for requested references or criteria and for requested response group</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Request_for_Quote" type="wd:Request_for_Quote_OutboundType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Wrapper element for Request for Quote Reference and Request for Quote Data.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Request_for_Quote_OutboundType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Wrapper element for Request for Quote Reference and Request for Quote Data.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Request_for_Quote_Reference" type="wd:Request_for_QuoteObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Request for Quote Reference.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Request_for_Quote_Data" type="wd:Request_for_Quote_DataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Request for Quote Data.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Request_for_Quote_DataType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Element that contains Request for Quote Data.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Enter a RFQ End Date that is after the Start Date.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Invite at least one supplier to bid on this RFQ.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Enter a RFQ Start Date that is on or after the Document Date.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Currency Conversion Rates between currency and company's default currency are not defined.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Enter unique suppliers to participate in this RFQ.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Request_for_Quote_ID" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Request for Quote Reference ID.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Invalid Request for Quote ID.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Submit" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Submit for Approval is a boolean flag indicating if the transaction is to be submitted or saved in draft mode. If this flag is set, the transaction will be submitted, otherwise the transaction is saved in draft.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="RFQ_Number" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Request for Quote Number.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="RFQ_Status_Reference" type="wd:Document_StatusObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to the Document Status for the Request for Quote. This field is read-only, and will be ignored on a Put or Submit.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Company_Reference" type="wd:CompanyObjectType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Company Reference</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="RFQ_Type_Reference" type="wd:Request_for_Quote_TypeObjectType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Request for Quote Type Reference.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Title" type="xsd:string" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Request for Quote Title.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Document_Date" type="xsd:date" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The date of the Request for Quote.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="RFQ_Start_Date" type="xsd:dateTime" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Request for Quote Start Date with time precision up to minute.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="RFQ_End_Date" type="xsd:dateTime" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Request for Quote End Date with time precision up to minute.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Time_Zone_Reference" type="wd:Time_ZoneObjectType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Time Zone for RFQ Start Date and RFQ End Date.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Currency_Reference" type="wd:CurrencyObjectType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Currency Reference</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Sourcing_Buyer_Reference" type="wd:WorkerObjectType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to Sourcing Buyer of Request for Quote.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Specify a valid Sourcing Buyer. The Sourcing Buyer must be an authorized buyer that is not terminated.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Exclude_Target_Price" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Exclude Target Price.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Request_for_Quote_Terms_and_Conditions" type="wd:RichText" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Request for Quote Terms and Conditions.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Memo" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Memo</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Request_for_Quote_Line_Data" type="wd:Request_for_Quote_Line_DataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Request for Quote Line Data.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>All Requisition line references should be part of the same requisition.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Request_for_Quote_Participant_List_Data" type="wd:Request_for_Quote_Participant_List_DataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Proposed Suppliers for the Request for Quote at header level.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Request_for_Quote_Bid_Requirement_Data" type="wd:Request_for_Quote_Bid_Requirement_DataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Request for Quote Bid Requirement Data.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Business_Document_Attachment_Data" type="wd:Business_Document_Attachment_with_External_Option_DataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Request_for_Quote_Line_DataType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Element that contains Request for Quote line data.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Enter a Line End Date that is after the Line Start Date.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Enter a Line Start Date that is on or after the RFQ Document Date.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Enter a Line End Date that is on or after the RFQ Document Date.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Enter an Item or Item Description on the RFQ Service Line.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Line Numbers need to be unique with in an RFQ document. Duplicate line number is [line number].</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Service Lines cannot be split based on quantity.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Total of Extended Amount in RFQ line splits are not same as Extended Amount for RFQ Line [Line Number].</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Quantity and Unit of Measure are required for Goods Line with Line Number [line number]</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Extended Amount is automatically calculated for Request for Quote Goods Line. If value is present, it should be equal to Unit Cost multiplied by Quantity. The Goods Line having incorrect value for extended amount is with Line Number [Line Number].</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Total of Quantity in RFQ line splits are not same as Quantity for RFQ Goods Line [Line Number].</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Quantity cannot be zero or negative for Goods Line Number [Line Number].</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Extended Amount is required and must have a value for Request for Quote Service Line Number [Line Number].</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Values for Start Date and End Date are not allowed for Goods Lines. The line number in error is [Line Number].</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Values for Quantity, Unit of Measure, Lead Time Required and Unit Cost are not allowed for Service Lines. The line number in error is [Line Number]</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Unit Cost cannot be zero or negative on Goods Line [line number].</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>[list of worktag types] not valid for this transaction.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Only one worktag for each type is allowed for each document line.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Spend Category on RFQ Line [line number] does not match the spend category for item [item].</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>A Spend Category is required on RFQ Line [line number].</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Enter a Requested Delivery Date that is on or after the RFQ Document Date.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Spend category "[spend category]" is inactive.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Request_for_Quote_Line_ID" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Request for Quote Line Reference ID.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Invalid Request for Quote Line ID.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Request_for_Quote_Line_Reference" type="wd:Request_for_Quote_LineObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Request for Quote Line Reference.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Line_Type_Reference" type="wd:Request_for_Quote_Line_TypeObjectType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Line Type Reference</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Requisition_Line_Reference" type="wd:Requisition_LineObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The Requisition Line sourced to the Request for Quote Line. This field is read only.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Requisition line cannot be sourced via the RFQ process or it is already referenced in another RFQ document.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't create a Request for Quote for a requisition with a strategic sourcing project assigned to it.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>You can't create a Request for Quote (RFQ) for a requisition without any existing RFQs, when the Tenant option Create Sourcing Projects Automatically when Requisition Lines are RFQ required is enabled.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Line_Number" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Line Number</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="5"/>
<xsd:minInclusive value="0"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="0"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Item_Reference" type="wd:Purchase_ItemObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Item Reference</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Item_Description" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Item Description</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Spend_Category_Reference" type="wd:Spend_CategoryObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Spend Category Reference</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Quantity" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Quantity</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="22"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="2"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Unit_of_Measure_Reference" type="wd:Unit_of_MeasureObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Unit of Measure Reference</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Unit_Cost" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Unit Cost</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="26"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="6"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Extended_Amount" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The Extended Amount for the RFQ Goods line. This amount is automatically calculated by multiplying the Quantity by the Unit Cost in the currency specified on the Goods Line.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="18"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="3"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Target_Price" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Target Price.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="18"/>
<xsd:minInclusive value="0"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="3"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Requested_Delivery_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Requested Delivery Date</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Start_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Start Date</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="End_Date" type="xsd:date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>End Date</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Response_Required" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Flag to indicate whether the line needs to be in present when processing RFQ Response.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Unit_Price_Required" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Price Required.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Lead_Time_Required" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Lead Time Required.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Worktags_Reference" type="wd:Accounting_WorktagObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Worktag Reference</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Worktags are not allowed when there are split lines.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>[list of worktag types] not valid for this transaction.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>[not allowed worktag types on Spend Transactions]</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The [type] is/are not available for use with the company/s: [partitionable] [company]</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>[worktag value] is not permitted as an allowed value for worktag type: [worktag type], because it is inactive.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Select a balancing worktag for Worktags of the following type: [type]</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The following Accounting Worktags are required but have not been assigned: [missing].</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>[missing required worktag types on Spend Transactions]</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>[invalid worktag value message]</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Memo" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Line Memo</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Request_for_Quote_Line_Bid_Requirement_Data" type="wd:Request_for_Quote_Line_Bid_Requirement_DataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Request for Quote Bid Requirement Data.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Request_for_Quote_Line_Split_Data" type="wd:Request_for_Quote_Line_Splits_DataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Request for Quote Line Split Data</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Business_Document_Line_Attachment_Data" type="wd:Business_Document_Attachment_with_External_Option_DataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Request_for_Quote_Line_Bid_Requirement_DataType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Wrapper element that has the bid requirements at Request for Quote line level.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Sequence_Number" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Sequence Number.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="5"/>
<xsd:minInclusive value="0"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="0"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Name" type="xsd:string" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Name.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Type_Reference" type="wd:Request_for_Quote_Bid_Requirement_TypeObjectType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Type of response for this bid requirement. Allowed types Date, Numeric and Text.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Response_Required" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Response Required for the bid question.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Memo" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Memo for the bid requirement.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Request_for_Quote_Participant_List_DataType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Element that contains the proposed suppliers for the Request for Quote at header level.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Supplier_Reference" type="wd:Resource_ProviderObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Supplier reference.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Suppliers that are restricted to company must be restricted to either the document header company or the Company Hierarchy for which it is a subordinate.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Issue_Option_Reference" type="wd:Purchase_Order_Issue_OptionObjectType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Issue Option for RFQ Participant.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>[Issue Option] issue option not supported by Supplier [supplier].</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Override_Contact_Email_Reference" type="wd:Unique_IdentifierObjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Email address of RFQ Participant.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Override Internet Email Address are allowed only for suppliers with Email issue option.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Request_for_Quote_Bid_Requirement_DataType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Element that contains the Request for Quote bid requirement data at header level.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Sequence_Number" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Sequence Number.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="5"/>
<xsd:minInclusive value="0"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="0"/>
</xsd:restriction>
</xsd:simpleType>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Name" type="xsd:string" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Name.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Type_Reference" type="wd:Request_for_Quote_Bid_Requirement_TypeObjectType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Type of response for this bid requirement. Allowed types Date, Numeric and Text.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Response_Required" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Response Required for the bid question.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Request_for_Quote_Bid_Requirement_Classification_Reference" type="wd:Request_for_Quote_Bid_Requirement_ClassificationObjectType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Request for Quote Bid Requirement Classification Reference.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Memo" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Memo for the bid requirement.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Item_Identifier_Type_Request_ReferencesType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The element containing item identifier type request references.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Item_Identifier_Type_Reference" type="wd:Item_Identifier_TypeObjectType" maxOccurs="unbounded">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The reference to item identifier type.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Item_Identifier_Type_Request_CriteriaType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The element containing item identifier type request criteria.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Item_Identifier_Type_Response_GroupType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The element containing item identifier type response group.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:element name="Include_Reference" type="xsd:boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Flag indicating whether to include reference or not.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
</xsd:complexType>
<xsd:complexType name="Get_Item_Identifier_Types_RequestType">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The element containing get item identifier types request.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:sequence>
<xsd:choice>
<xsd:element name="Request_References" type="wd:Item_Identifier_Type_Request_ReferencesType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The item identifier type references element contains the instances of item identifier types.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Request_Criteria" type="wd:Item_Identifier_Type_Request_CriteriaType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The element containing item identifier type request criteria.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:choice>
<xsd:element name="Response_Filter" type="wd:Response_FilterType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The parameters that let you filter the data returned in the response. You can filter returned data by entry date time and page attributes.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Response_Group" type="wd:Item_Identifier_Type_Response_GroupType" minOccurs="0">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>The element containing the item identifier type response group.</xsd:documentation>
</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
</xsd:sequence>
