</xsd:annotation>
</xsd:element>
<xsd:element name="Proposed_Useful_Life" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
<xsd:annotation>
<xsd:documentation>Reference to Useful Life for the specified book.</xsd:documentation>
<xsd:appinfo>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Enter a Useful Life that is more than the number of periods that the asset has depreciated as of the transaction effective date.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>When depreciation is based on the number of days per period, all the fiscal years / periods for an asset's useful life must already be created in order to calculate the depreciation amount for each period correctly. In order to complete the accounting setup for this asset, you will first need to create additional fiscal years / periods for the fiscal schedule of this asset's company.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>Useful life must be greater than zero.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The useful life of [Asset] can't be changed in the [Book] book because it uses a term or declining balance depreciation method. You must set the proposed useful life to the original useful life of [Original Useful Life] periods.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation>
<wd:Validation_Message>The useful life of [Asset] can't be changed because the asset was added as fully depreciated in the [Book] book. You must set the proposed useful life to the original useful life of [Original Useful Life] periods.</wd:Validation_Message>
</wd:Validation>
</xsd:appinfo>
</xsd:annotation>
<xsd:simpleType>
<xsd:restriction base="xsd:decimal">
<xsd:totalDigits value="12"/>
<xsd:minInclusive value="0"/>
<xsd:fractionDigits value="0"/>
